1
00:00:01,027 --> 00:00:04,667
(Early Merry Christmas)

2
00:00:05,537 --> 00:00:08,407
(Christmas is nearing for the Rainbow Club too.)

3
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:10,366
Nice to see you all.

4
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:12,707
(Nice to see you.)

5
00:00:13,077 --> 00:00:14,376
It's the warm and cozy time at the end of the year.

6
00:00:14,377 --> 00:00:15,846
For the year-end vibe,

7
00:00:15,847 --> 00:00:18,917
we prepared the best cakes of the cakes, the ice cream cakes.

8
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:22,616
- They're ice cream cakes. - You didn't know they were, right?

9
00:00:22,617 --> 00:00:23,646
They look so beautiful.

10
00:00:23,647 --> 00:00:26,016
Wrap up the year on a good note. It's the cozy time of the year.

11
00:00:26,017 --> 00:00:27,156
- Let's blow out... - Okay.

12
00:00:27,157 --> 00:00:28,257
The candles together.

13
00:00:28,387 --> 00:00:30,587
One, two, three.

14
00:00:31,157 --> 00:00:32,157
(Blowing out the candles)

15
00:00:32,158 --> 00:00:33,996
Happy New Year.

16
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:35,297
Happy New Year.

17
00:00:35,597 --> 00:00:36,866
This is creme brulee.

18
00:00:36,867 --> 00:00:38,437
It's fun to crack the cake. See?

19
00:00:38,837 --> 00:00:39,897
This is fun.

20
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:42,407
Like this.

21
00:00:42,937 --> 00:00:44,777
(Taking a bite)

22
00:00:45,407 --> 00:00:46,476
(A sweet flavor spreads in his mouth.)

23
00:00:46,477 --> 00:00:48,477
You must have the ice cream with the creme brulee.

24
00:00:49,207 --> 00:00:50,477
This one is good.

25
00:00:50,707 --> 00:00:51,747
It's good.

26
00:00:52,017 --> 00:00:54,193
- Let's try this too. - There are two different flavors.

27
00:00:54,217 --> 00:00:55,316
(Taking a bite)

28
00:00:55,317 --> 00:00:57,587
Kian84 is indeed on a different level.

29
00:00:57,747 --> 00:00:58,857
(Fascinated)

30
00:00:59,117 --> 00:01:01,486
(Let us take a bite of it too.)

31
00:01:01,487 --> 00:01:03,326
This reminds me of hot chocolate.

32
00:01:03,327 --> 00:01:05,473
- It's basically hot chocolate. - It tastes like hot chocolate.

33
00:01:05,497 --> 00:01:07,156
Gosh, you have ice cream all over your chin.

34
00:01:07,157 --> 00:01:08,166
Really?

35
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:09,997
- I guess you really like it. - It's good.

36
00:01:10,927 --> 00:01:11,967
My gosh. Come on.

37
00:01:12,497 --> 00:01:14,467
- This was a nice energy boost. - Yes.

38
00:01:14,967 --> 00:01:16,487
Let's jump right into today's episode.

39
00:01:17,167 --> 00:01:18,376
The member we'll meet this week...

40
00:01:18,377 --> 00:01:20,406
has enough passion that can turn the coldest winter...

41
00:01:20,407 --> 00:01:22,307
- into the hottest summer. - Yes.

42
00:01:22,477 --> 00:01:24,677
He's the icon of fiery charisma.

43
00:01:24,877 --> 00:01:26,377
Let's watch the clip to find out!

44
00:01:28,387 --> 00:01:29,746
(Bring It On, Ghost)

45
00:01:29,747 --> 00:01:31,627
- "Bring It On, Ghost?" - "Bring It On, Ghost?"

46
00:01:32,617 --> 00:01:34,617
- Gosh, it's cold. - He's wearing workout clothes.

47
00:01:34,687 --> 00:01:36,327
He's always wearing workout clothes.

48
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:38,396
They look different from his usual workout clothes.

49
00:01:38,397 --> 00:01:39,427
- Really? - Yes.

50
00:01:40,197 --> 00:01:41,696
(Current time: 7am)

51
00:01:41,697 --> 00:01:44,227
People leave that early in the morning for marathons.

52
00:01:45,037 --> 00:01:46,767
Gosh, what's taking them so long?

53
00:01:48,437 --> 00:01:49,906
(He keeps pacing back and forth as it's cold.)

54
00:01:49,907 --> 00:01:51,107
Is he waiting for someone?

55
00:01:52,677 --> 00:01:53,776
(It's freezing.)

56
00:01:53,777 --> 00:01:55,447
It was freezing that day.

57
00:01:55,677 --> 00:01:57,976
It was a cold day. The temperature was minus 5°C.

58
00:01:57,977 --> 00:01:59,747
(Shaking)

59
00:02:03,617 --> 00:02:05,017
We have a long way to go.

60
00:02:07,157 --> 00:02:10,657
(He keeps waiting for someone.)

61
00:02:13,227 --> 00:02:15,096
- Come on, guys. - "Guys?"

62
00:02:15,097 --> 00:02:16,097
(Lightening up)

63
00:02:17,327 --> 00:02:18,437
Someone's here.

64
00:02:19,137 --> 00:02:20,466
Come on, guys.

65
00:02:20,467 --> 00:02:21,867
(A car pulls up in front of MINHO.)

66
00:02:22,107 --> 00:02:23,267
Do you know what time it is?

67
00:02:24,307 --> 00:02:25,537
It's been a while.

68
00:02:26,977 --> 00:02:28,577
- Victory. - Victory.

69
00:02:29,207 --> 00:02:30,247
At ease.

70
00:02:31,147 --> 00:02:32,716
- It's been a while. - Who are they?

71
00:02:32,717 --> 00:02:34,516
He saluted and said, "victory." Isn't it obvious?

72
00:02:34,517 --> 00:02:36,017
- The Marines? - Let's go.

73
00:02:36,647 --> 00:02:37,647
Victory.

74
00:02:37,648 --> 00:02:39,316
I'm Choi Min Ho from the 1,245th intake.

75
00:02:39,317 --> 00:02:40,416
"Victory."

76
00:02:40,417 --> 00:02:42,026
(Once a Marine, forever a Marine.)

77
00:02:42,027 --> 00:02:43,157
He looks sharp.

78
00:02:44,287 --> 00:02:46,557
- The uniform suits him. - He's so cool.

79
00:02:47,097 --> 00:02:48,726
Just looking at his face, I bet he was great in the Marines.

80
00:02:48,727 --> 00:02:49,967
- Gosh, of course. - Of course.

81
00:02:50,027 --> 00:02:52,187
I was in the 839th intake with the conscripted police.

82
00:02:53,637 --> 00:02:54,866
What about you, Hyun Moo?

83
00:02:54,867 --> 00:02:56,183
- You were in the KATUSA program. - I was in the KATUSA program.

84
00:02:56,207 --> 00:02:58,336
- I was with the 39th... - Do you know your number?

85
00:02:58,337 --> 00:03:00,406
(With the 39th...)

86
00:03:00,407 --> 00:03:01,706
- What was that? - With the 39th intake?

87
00:03:01,707 --> 00:03:03,006
No, I was just joking.

88
00:03:03,007 --> 00:03:04,553
- There weren't any numbers, right? - I don't know mine.

89
00:03:04,577 --> 00:03:05,676
- And let's be honest. - Does the army have that too?

90
00:03:05,677 --> 00:03:07,423
I bet you can't remember those days anymore.

91
00:03:07,447 --> 00:03:08,986
(It's hard to remember his days from the 20th century.)

92
00:03:08,987 --> 00:03:11,107
- I mean, even I... - It feels like my previous life.

93
00:03:11,517 --> 00:03:13,363
- Where did you serve? - I was with the Korea Coast Guard.

94
00:03:13,387 --> 00:03:14,926
- Korea Coast Guard? - From Mokpo?

95
00:03:14,927 --> 00:03:16,727
- We all served in different places. - Right.

96
00:03:16,957 --> 00:03:18,573
- Conscripted police, Coast Guard, - Yes.

97
00:03:18,597 --> 00:03:19,696
- I was with the Marine Corps. - Marine Corps,

98
00:03:19,697 --> 00:03:21,357
- Army. KATUSA. - army, and KATUSA.

99
00:03:21,697 --> 00:03:23,067
This rarely happens.

100
00:03:23,197 --> 00:03:26,036
- You didn't serve? - Should I join the National Guard?

101
00:03:26,037 --> 00:03:27,197
(Me?)

102
00:03:27,897 --> 00:03:28,966
"You didn't serve?"

103
00:03:28,967 --> 00:03:30,207
Gosh, this is awkward.

104
00:03:30,307 --> 00:03:32,236
- She graduated from SNU. - Right, Seoul National University.

105
00:03:32,237 --> 00:03:33,536
- SNU. - That's the most prestigious one.

106
00:03:33,537 --> 00:03:35,937
- The most prestigious one. - She supervises people like us.

107
00:03:36,077 --> 00:03:37,277
- That's right. - Right.

108
00:03:37,477 --> 00:03:39,177
- She's the mastermind. - Yes.

109
00:03:39,947 --> 00:03:41,316
- The car... - Gosh, it's so cold.

110
00:03:41,317 --> 00:03:42,917
What took you so long?

111
00:03:43,117 --> 00:03:44,837
- What's this? - We tried to get here fast.

112
00:03:45,357 --> 00:03:48,487
- They're my dear comrades. - Have you been well?

113
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:50,027
Why didn't you bundle up more?

114
00:03:50,227 --> 00:03:52,227
Hey, I thought my ears were going to fall off.

115
00:03:52,697 --> 00:03:56,097
The three of us made good memories over the years.

116
00:03:56,367 --> 00:03:58,247
They're younger than me, were above me in rank.

117
00:03:58,367 --> 00:03:59,766
I started my day with them.

118
00:03:59,767 --> 00:04:02,207
- I enlisted rather late. - You enlisted late.

119
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:04,636
We went through tough times together.

120
00:04:04,637 --> 00:04:06,106
So we've bonded more.

121
00:04:06,107 --> 00:04:08,153
Once we finished our service, we became good friends.

122
00:04:08,177 --> 00:04:10,506
("MINHO Joins Final Training Instead of Taking His Day Off")

123
00:04:10,507 --> 00:04:11,947
Why didn't you take your day off?

124
00:04:12,517 --> 00:04:13,517
Why did you do that?

125
00:04:13,518 --> 00:04:16,147
Around the time of my discharge,

126
00:04:16,287 --> 00:04:18,216
a major field-training exercise was scheduled.

127
00:04:18,217 --> 00:04:19,563
It was called Homeland Defense Training.

128
00:04:19,587 --> 00:04:21,956
I really wanted to take part in that.

129
00:04:21,957 --> 00:04:24,026
You know what? Even when you're determined...

130
00:04:24,027 --> 00:04:26,097
- not to participate, - That's impressive.

131
00:04:26,227 --> 00:04:28,226
- once you see your juniors... - Seriously. That's amazing.

132
00:04:28,227 --> 00:04:29,526
(Once you see your juniors, you can't just walk away.)

133
00:04:29,527 --> 00:04:31,126
- That's how I felt. - Right.

134
00:04:31,127 --> 00:04:33,036
I thought, "Yes. I should..."

135
00:04:33,037 --> 00:04:34,573
- "make one last good memory." - Right.

136
00:04:34,597 --> 00:04:36,367
He'd only work out on his days off anyway.

137
00:04:37,207 --> 00:04:38,753
- It didn't matter where he was. - He'd be doing the same thing.

138
00:04:38,777 --> 00:04:40,507
- You're spot on. - But...

139
00:04:40,777 --> 00:04:42,506
Even after we got discharged,

140
00:04:42,507 --> 00:04:45,246
we naturally kept in touch and spent time together.

141
00:04:45,247 --> 00:04:47,777
So we also went on a trip together.

142
00:04:48,277 --> 00:04:49,946
I bet you guys are really close.

143
00:04:49,947 --> 00:04:51,716
It's impossible not to bond.

144
00:04:51,717 --> 00:04:55,227
About 20 to 30 people still gather when we hang out together...

145
00:04:55,427 --> 00:04:57,057
- from time to time. - Really?

146
00:04:57,427 --> 00:04:58,597
They were above me in rank.

147
00:04:58,997 --> 00:05:02,396
But we're still good friends once we got out.

148
00:05:02,397 --> 00:05:03,866
- My gosh. - Here we go.

149
00:05:03,867 --> 00:05:04,927
Let's go.

150
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:09,067
Seeing you guys is bringing back old memories.

151
00:05:09,507 --> 00:05:12,077
It's been a while since we're going on a trip.

152
00:05:12,537 --> 00:05:14,337
I didn't even get to sleep for an hour today.

153
00:05:14,537 --> 00:05:16,546
We were going on a trip together.

154
00:05:16,547 --> 00:05:17,547
I was excited,

155
00:05:17,548 --> 00:05:18,846
- so it was hard to fall asleep. - I bet.

156
00:05:18,847 --> 00:05:20,376
- I fell asleep... - The World Cup Draw.

157
00:05:20,377 --> 00:05:21,886
While watching the World Cup Draw.

158
00:05:21,887 --> 00:05:23,847
Gosh, Korea is in a nice group.

159
00:05:24,617 --> 00:05:26,587
I miss the executive officer.

160
00:05:27,117 --> 00:05:28,886
- We should go and see him. - Is he in Pohang now?

161
00:05:28,887 --> 00:05:29,927
He's in Pohang.

162
00:05:30,487 --> 00:05:31,686
He's at the Airborne Training Center.

163
00:05:31,687 --> 00:05:33,396
It's been five years since your discharge.

164
00:05:33,397 --> 00:05:35,367
- You still keep in touch with them? - Yes.

165
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:37,527
I went to his house once a long time ago.

166
00:05:37,697 --> 00:05:39,666
His wife gave us this half-dried saury salad.

167
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:41,496
- Gosh. - It was so good.

168
00:05:41,497 --> 00:05:45,507
He sends us half-dried saury when it's in season.

169
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:46,707
Seriously.

170
00:05:47,177 --> 00:05:48,847
Didn't we visit him last year?

171
00:05:49,577 --> 00:05:50,646
We saw him...

172
00:05:50,647 --> 00:05:51,876
- more than once every year. - Right.

173
00:05:51,877 --> 00:05:53,316
We went to Gangwon Province...

174
00:05:53,317 --> 00:05:54,717
- and Incheon. - Right.

175
00:05:54,877 --> 00:05:56,287
You guys do meet often.

176
00:05:56,317 --> 00:05:58,617
(Glancing)

177
00:05:58,717 --> 00:06:02,727
You're used to driving the kids around.

178
00:06:03,087 --> 00:06:04,427
You're a smooth driver.

179
00:06:04,927 --> 00:06:06,626
- He's a father? - No.

180
00:06:06,627 --> 00:06:08,526
- He's a taekwondo instructor. Yes. - He is?

181
00:06:08,527 --> 00:06:10,097
Gosh, he's a taekwondo instructor.

182
00:06:10,397 --> 00:06:13,296
When I worked as an art teacher, I used to drive the academy bus too.

183
00:06:13,297 --> 00:06:14,566
- Really? - Really?

184
00:06:14,567 --> 00:06:16,536
The director asked me if I could drive the bus...

185
00:06:16,537 --> 00:06:17,706
on top of teaching them.

186
00:06:17,707 --> 00:06:19,736
(Nudging him to take an extra rask)

187
00:06:19,737 --> 00:06:21,206
I was like, "Hey, get in now."

188
00:06:21,207 --> 00:06:22,576
- You had multiple tasks. - Multiple tasks.

189
00:06:22,577 --> 00:06:23,977
The job was killing me.

190
00:06:25,647 --> 00:06:28,277
Are you hogging up all the attention from the mothers?

191
00:06:28,717 --> 00:06:29,986
I'm you at the taekwondo center.

192
00:06:29,987 --> 00:06:32,287
(I'm you at the taekwondo center.)

193
00:06:32,687 --> 00:06:33,786
He's easy-going.

194
00:06:33,787 --> 00:06:36,357
You're still working there. You didn't quit.

195
00:06:36,887 --> 00:06:39,097
- Did you get a girlfriend? - No.

196
00:06:40,097 --> 00:06:41,326
How long has it been then?

197
00:06:41,327 --> 00:06:42,697
No, MINHO. I had one before.

198
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:44,396
Stop lying.

199
00:06:44,397 --> 00:06:47,336
- Because I never met her... - You think I'm always lying, right?

200
00:06:47,337 --> 00:06:49,897
- Come on. Because I never met... - Why do you think he's lying?

201
00:06:49,937 --> 00:06:51,466
- I know... - No, I had a girlfriend.

202
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:52,977
All about their dating history.

203
00:06:53,137 --> 00:06:55,976
Have you still not gotten over your first love?

204
00:06:55,977 --> 00:06:58,677
Gosh, no. Besides, she's not my first love.

205
00:06:59,217 --> 00:07:01,493
It feels like only yesterday he was telling me about his love troubles.

206
00:07:01,517 --> 00:07:02,786
She's getting married soon.

207
00:07:02,787 --> 00:07:03,917
- Really? - Yes.

208
00:07:05,287 --> 00:07:06,517
Wait. Who? Your first love?

209
00:07:06,787 --> 00:07:08,417
- She's not my first love. - She's not.

210
00:07:08,627 --> 00:07:11,127
From what I remember, a lot of people told MINHO...

211
00:07:11,527 --> 00:07:13,627
about their love troubles.

212
00:07:13,727 --> 00:07:16,026
People who were above me in rank came to me and asked my opinion...

213
00:07:16,027 --> 00:07:18,566
about their future plans once they got discharged.

214
00:07:18,567 --> 00:07:20,443
- They asked me for my advice. - Right. A lot of people did.

215
00:07:20,467 --> 00:07:21,566
You're older than us, after all.

216
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:24,007
Asking the older guys is natural when you're in the military.

217
00:07:24,237 --> 00:07:27,577
They came to me when they had exactly a month left.

218
00:07:27,937 --> 00:07:29,746
And they told me about their life plans.

219
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:31,076
- Really? - Right.

220
00:07:31,077 --> 00:07:33,576
- I was Dr. Oh Eun Yeong in there. - I bet.

221
00:07:33,577 --> 00:07:34,616
Seriously.

222
00:07:34,617 --> 00:07:37,587
- Our station had a good vibe. - We had a great vibe.

223
00:07:38,287 --> 00:07:40,986
(They keep sharing stories about their military service.)

224
00:07:40,987 --> 00:07:41,987
I bet it's fun.

225
00:07:41,988 --> 00:07:44,286
When I meet my co-stars from plays again,

226
00:07:44,287 --> 00:07:45,726
we always talk about the same thing.

227
00:07:45,727 --> 00:07:47,026
- Right. - But we really like doing that.

228
00:07:47,027 --> 00:07:49,867
- Right. That's what we need. - A bit of trouble makes it fun.

229
00:07:50,127 --> 00:07:51,197
Daegwallyeong.

230
00:07:51,297 --> 00:07:52,537
They drove to Gangwon Province.

231
00:07:52,997 --> 00:07:54,877
I knew it. Spending time with fellow Marines...

232
00:07:55,367 --> 00:07:57,047
makes one and a half hours fly by so fast.

233
00:07:58,537 --> 00:07:59,707
I think we're almost there.

234
00:08:01,207 --> 00:08:02,247
This is the place.

235
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:04,677
- Okay. Let's go. - We're here. Yes.

236
00:08:05,007 --> 00:08:06,417
Gangwon Province.

237
00:08:08,987 --> 00:08:10,647
Where is this place? A service area?

238
00:08:12,187 --> 00:08:13,456
If it weren't windy today...

239
00:08:13,457 --> 00:08:14,663
(Did the Marine trio get out at the service area?)

240
00:08:14,687 --> 00:08:16,127
There he is.

241
00:08:16,887 --> 00:08:17,926
(Laughing out loud)

242
00:08:17,927 --> 00:08:20,633
- They're meeting up with someone. - They're meeting with more people.

243
00:08:20,657 --> 00:08:22,367
- Lee Gi Mo. - Victory.

244
00:08:22,427 --> 00:08:23,497
Victory.

245
00:08:24,567 --> 00:08:26,596
(A man gives a disciplined salute.)

246
00:08:26,597 --> 00:08:27,897
- How cute. - He looks cute.

247
00:08:28,567 --> 00:08:29,867
I'm his favorite Marine.

248
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:33,236
I finally met my fellow Marine who was right below me in rank.

249
00:08:33,237 --> 00:08:34,406
(Marine Lee Gi Mo, a direct junior of MINHO)

250
00:08:34,407 --> 00:08:35,477
How old is he?

251
00:08:35,577 --> 00:08:37,107
- He was born in 1998. - What?

252
00:08:38,207 --> 00:08:40,047
He must've worked really hard in the military.

253
00:08:41,417 --> 00:08:43,086
You might not know just by looking at him,

254
00:08:43,087 --> 00:08:44,717
- but he has two kids. - My gosh.

255
00:08:45,557 --> 00:08:47,416
- I see. - He's the most mature one then.

256
00:08:47,417 --> 00:08:49,286
- Yes, in a way, he's our senior. - He's everyone's senior.

257
00:08:49,287 --> 00:08:50,387
Right.

258
00:08:51,857 --> 00:08:53,897
- He turned 27 this year, right? - Yes.

259
00:08:55,027 --> 00:08:56,027
(MINHO, Gi Mo)

260
00:08:56,028 --> 00:08:59,397
(He's the only junior of MINHO in today's group.)

261
00:08:59,667 --> 00:09:02,907
The two seniors I met earlier...

262
00:09:03,307 --> 00:09:04,707
enlisted before me.

263
00:09:05,277 --> 00:09:08,477
So being with them was both comfortable and uncomfortable.

264
00:09:08,747 --> 00:09:10,107
But as for Gi Mo,

265
00:09:10,347 --> 00:09:12,777
he's my direct junior.

266
00:09:13,047 --> 00:09:14,116
I can do whatever I want.

267
00:09:14,117 --> 00:09:16,357
(Choi Min Ho: 1,245th intake, Lee Gi Mo: 1,246th intake)

268
00:09:16,517 --> 00:09:19,917
Gi Mo and I served the longest together.

269
00:09:20,287 --> 00:09:22,756
- He's your go-to guy. - Yes, he is.

270
00:09:22,757 --> 00:09:24,157
He's your own Wilson.

271
00:09:24,787 --> 00:09:26,257
I brought him everywhere.

272
00:09:26,557 --> 00:09:29,097
Poor guy. He ended up with the wrong senior.

273
00:09:30,397 --> 00:09:33,566
Gi Mo is from Gangwon Province.

274
00:09:33,567 --> 00:09:34,596
He was born and raised there.

275
00:09:34,597 --> 00:09:36,867
So when we were training in Pohang,

276
00:09:37,207 --> 00:09:39,206
he always said that he'd take care of everything...

277
00:09:39,207 --> 00:09:41,177
if we came to Gangwon Province.

278
00:09:41,537 --> 00:09:42,707
Everyone says that.

279
00:09:43,377 --> 00:09:45,817
So we actually went to Gangwon Province on a trip...

280
00:09:45,917 --> 00:09:47,176
to catch up.

281
00:09:47,177 --> 00:09:48,617
We had a blast on the trip too.

282
00:09:48,787 --> 00:09:51,447
We decided to follow his lead and came to Gangwon Province again.

283
00:09:52,557 --> 00:09:54,017
It's been a while.

284
00:09:54,617 --> 00:09:57,057
(Not moving)

285
00:09:57,657 --> 00:10:00,457
My gosh. He's not lowering his hand. This is so stressful.

286
00:10:01,457 --> 00:10:03,377
The junior can't lower it until the senior does.

287
00:10:03,697 --> 00:10:05,837
See? This isn't right.

288
00:10:06,137 --> 00:10:07,737
Even his seniors aren't doing it.

289
00:10:10,007 --> 00:10:11,107
At ease.

290
00:10:13,337 --> 00:10:15,446
(As he was happy to see Gi Mo, the salute took a long time.)

291
00:10:15,447 --> 00:10:18,847
Wait. Gi Mo has a big build.

292
00:10:18,977 --> 00:10:20,717
- He's tall. - Yes, he's tall.

293
00:10:21,047 --> 00:10:23,117
- Let's go inside. It's cold. - Let's go inside.

294
00:10:23,887 --> 00:10:25,986
- Have you been well? - Yes, sir. Have you been well?

295
00:10:25,987 --> 00:10:27,817
Your hair grew a bit.

296
00:10:27,917 --> 00:10:29,057
- Really? - Yes.

297
00:10:29,427 --> 00:10:32,856
He's still showing his respect to you as his senior.

298
00:10:32,857 --> 00:10:35,097
- We do that to tease each other. - To tease each other?

299
00:10:36,397 --> 00:10:38,027
We're in Gi Mo's hometown.

300
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,467
First of all,

301
00:10:41,097 --> 00:10:43,836
we'll have some simple snacks at the top.

302
00:10:43,837 --> 00:10:45,267
Can we buy ramyeon?

303
00:10:45,437 --> 00:10:47,157
- Ramyeon sounds good. - Let's get ramyeon.

304
00:10:47,877 --> 00:10:51,107
Today, I wanted us to get a taste of our old days...

305
00:10:51,447 --> 00:10:53,346
or our old hardships, per se.

306
00:10:53,347 --> 00:10:57,047
Our basic training was marching.

307
00:10:57,547 --> 00:10:58,787
So we decided to hike.

308
00:10:59,387 --> 00:11:01,187
- Why would you do that? - I see.

309
00:11:01,317 --> 00:11:02,527
Gi Mo came up...

310
00:11:02,827 --> 00:11:05,457
with this hiking trail on Seonjaryeong.

311
00:11:06,097 --> 00:11:07,197
What do you want to eat?

312
00:11:07,927 --> 00:11:10,027
- We can just pick the one we want. - Yes.

313
00:11:11,097 --> 00:11:12,366
I'll go with this.

314
00:11:12,367 --> 00:11:13,597
I like spicy ramyeon.

315
00:11:14,097 --> 00:11:16,007
- I... - Gi Mo can't eat spicy food.

316
00:11:16,237 --> 00:11:17,537
I'll go with beef-bone noodles.

317
00:11:18,067 --> 00:11:20,777
(Finding him cute)

318
00:11:21,237 --> 00:11:23,507
- Is this all? Do you want... - That's it.

319
00:11:23,807 --> 00:11:24,876
- Really? This is it? - Yes.

320
00:11:24,877 --> 00:11:26,217
- Are you sure? Okay. - Yes.

321
00:11:26,517 --> 00:11:27,577
Let's go and pay.

322
00:11:27,917 --> 00:11:30,616
I can tell that MINHO likes...

323
00:11:30,617 --> 00:11:31,986
- I can see he likes Gi Mo. - Right.

324
00:11:31,987 --> 00:11:33,863
- He takes good care of Gi Mo. - Gi Mo is his go-to guy.

325
00:11:33,887 --> 00:11:35,216
- That's... - Have a good day.

326
00:11:35,217 --> 00:11:37,627
- Can we get some hot water? - Sure.

327
00:11:37,787 --> 00:11:38,856
You brought it.

328
00:11:38,857 --> 00:11:40,903
- You're well-disciplined indeed. - Gosh. It's nothing.

329
00:11:40,927 --> 00:11:43,267
I knew it, Shim Chang Eon. You're well-prepared.

330
00:11:43,427 --> 00:11:46,697
To compliment someone, we say, "You're well-disciplined."

331
00:11:47,297 --> 00:11:48,767
Hey, it might be really heavy.

332
00:11:49,067 --> 00:11:50,883
Let's play rock-paper-scissors to decide who'll be carrying this.

333
00:11:50,907 --> 00:11:52,137
- All done. - Okay.

334
00:11:52,637 --> 00:11:53,707
Let's go.

335
00:11:54,837 --> 00:11:57,307
Everyone wore their combat boots.

336
00:11:57,477 --> 00:11:58,507
Of course.

337
00:11:59,417 --> 00:12:00,516
They're wearing combat boots.

338
00:12:00,517 --> 00:12:02,693
- They're wearing combat boots? - It looks like they're in training.

339
00:12:02,717 --> 00:12:04,447
I also brought mine too.

340
00:12:04,717 --> 00:12:07,087
We should all wear combat boots and hike.

341
00:12:07,417 --> 00:12:08,557
Hey, look at that.

342
00:12:08,927 --> 00:12:10,186
They're your combat boots...

343
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:11,856
- from five years ago? - Yes, they are my old combat boots.

344
00:12:11,857 --> 00:12:12,996
Gosh, they look so cute.

345
00:12:12,997 --> 00:12:15,497
- The military gives out good stuff. - They look cute.

346
00:12:16,167 --> 00:12:18,226
Everyone, make sure to have your gear.

347
00:12:18,227 --> 00:12:19,736
- Yes, sir. - Let's get changed.

348
00:12:19,737 --> 00:12:21,657
- Get changed. - They brought their uniform too.

349
00:12:22,137 --> 00:12:24,067
(I'm getting pumped up.)

350
00:12:25,337 --> 00:12:26,377
- How is it? - I'm good.

351
00:12:26,507 --> 00:12:27,537
This is good.

352
00:12:27,907 --> 00:12:28,977
I can handle it.

353
00:12:29,447 --> 00:12:30,477
Let's go.

354
00:12:30,847 --> 00:12:31,906
Let's go.

355
00:12:31,907 --> 00:12:34,847
It's so windy. They're not wearing a hat or gloves.

356
00:12:35,317 --> 00:12:36,917
Hey, won't your ears get too cold?

357
00:12:37,387 --> 00:12:38,487
We're the Marines.

358
00:12:38,817 --> 00:12:40,717
So the Marines' ears don't get cold?

359
00:12:40,987 --> 00:12:42,267
We overcome it with our passion.

360
00:12:43,227 --> 00:12:45,267
If it gets too cold, we can remove one of our ears.

361
00:12:45,457 --> 00:12:47,603
We're all pretentious a bit since we served in the Marines.

362
00:12:47,627 --> 00:12:49,867
Right. But that's the fun of it. That's why you meet up.

363
00:12:50,867 --> 00:12:52,797
- Is it this way? - I think it's this way.

364
00:12:53,267 --> 00:12:55,136
You guys don't need to stretch before the hike, right?

365
00:12:55,137 --> 00:12:56,306
- Of course. - We're good.

366
00:12:56,307 --> 00:12:57,587
(Today's hiking trail begins...)

367
00:12:58,107 --> 00:13:02,037
(from a small path next to the service area.)

368
00:13:02,177 --> 00:13:03,746
"Pyeongchang County Mountain Climbing Guide Map."

369
00:13:03,747 --> 00:13:04,747
There's the map.

370
00:13:05,077 --> 00:13:06,216
Let's take a look before we go.

371
00:13:06,217 --> 00:13:08,146
(Pyeongchang County Mountain Climbing Guide Map)

372
00:13:08,147 --> 00:13:09,546
This is where we are. We're headed to...

373
00:13:09,547 --> 00:13:10,987
- Seonjaryeong, right? - Yes.

374
00:13:11,287 --> 00:13:13,456
I think Seonjaryeong is famous among backpackers.

375
00:13:13,457 --> 00:13:14,487
- But... - Really?

376
00:13:14,587 --> 00:13:18,087
The altitude is 1,157m?

377
00:13:18,427 --> 00:13:20,556
The round trip is 11km? That's a piece of cake. Let's go.

378
00:13:20,557 --> 00:13:21,833
- How is that a piece of cake? - Let's go.

379
00:13:21,857 --> 00:13:26,897
The hiking trail reached an altitude of 1,100m.

380
00:13:27,267 --> 00:13:31,136
The distance was about 11km.

381
00:13:31,137 --> 00:13:33,377
An 11km hiking trail is considered really long.

382
00:13:33,877 --> 00:13:36,907
It said it usually took around 4.5 hours.

383
00:13:37,347 --> 00:13:40,517
But we were trained in military marching.

384
00:13:41,247 --> 00:13:44,446
I thought we could shorten that time by an hour when we began.

385
00:13:44,447 --> 00:13:46,517
(Highly motivated like a true Marine)

386
00:13:46,687 --> 00:13:48,157
- Okay. Let's go. - Let's go.

387
00:13:48,287 --> 00:13:49,826
But this isn't a trail running race.

388
00:13:49,827 --> 00:13:51,727
I perceived it as my own training exercise.

389
00:13:52,427 --> 00:13:54,026
- Sergeant Kim Tae Hwan. - Yes?

390
00:13:54,027 --> 00:13:55,827
Shouldn't you guide us?

391
00:13:56,227 --> 00:13:58,427
Why don't you show us how it's done? You're our senior.

392
00:13:58,797 --> 00:14:01,597
- One, two, three, four. - Gosh.

393
00:14:02,137 --> 00:14:04,406
Invincible Marines, shout it out. Go!

394
00:14:04,407 --> 00:14:06,436
My gosh, you remember that.

395
00:14:06,437 --> 00:14:07,777
- Of course. - Oh, my.

396
00:14:08,237 --> 00:14:09,983
- Why did he say it like that? - The drill instructors...

397
00:14:10,007 --> 00:14:11,476
- Why did he say it like that? - The drill instructors...

398
00:14:11,477 --> 00:14:12,946
don't want to lose their voice.

399
00:14:12,947 --> 00:14:14,247
- They keep doing this. - Right.

400
00:14:14,347 --> 00:14:16,186
- "Recruits!" - That's right.

401
00:14:16,187 --> 00:14:18,146
- They do this to keep their voice. - Their voice would go hoarse.

402
00:14:18,147 --> 00:14:19,756
That explains their vocalization.

403
00:14:19,757 --> 00:14:20,916
- They need to control their voice. - I see.

404
00:14:20,917 --> 00:14:22,326
"March." Like this.

405
00:14:22,327 --> 00:14:24,286
Invincible Marines, shout it out. Go!

406
00:14:24,287 --> 00:14:25,386
- I hate that sound. - I see.

407
00:14:25,387 --> 00:14:27,397
That way, they won't lose their voice.

408
00:14:27,927 --> 00:14:28,927
It's tough.

409
00:14:29,867 --> 00:14:31,667
It's been a while since you all hiked, right?

410
00:14:32,097 --> 00:14:33,366
- You too? - It's been a while for me too.

411
00:14:33,367 --> 00:14:34,396
- Everyone, right? - Right.

412
00:14:34,397 --> 00:14:36,066
Gi Mo, you said you came here two years ago.

413
00:14:36,067 --> 00:14:37,467
- I came here just once. - I see.

414
00:14:37,907 --> 00:14:39,876
- Gi Mo, no one gets left behind. - Yes, sir.

415
00:14:39,877 --> 00:14:41,577
That's right, sir! No!

416
00:14:43,607 --> 00:14:45,446
- He's only 27 years old? - He's 27.

417
00:14:45,447 --> 00:14:47,816
- I get why you keep teasing him. - Right.

418
00:14:47,817 --> 00:14:49,886
- He's adorable. - His reaction is fun to watch.

419
00:14:49,887 --> 00:14:51,546
- I love his reaction. - Yes.

420
00:14:51,547 --> 00:14:53,516
- That's why you hang out with them. - Right.

421
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:55,186
- You guys can't meet without him. - Gosh.

422
00:14:55,187 --> 00:14:56,427
Gi Mo has to join us.

423
00:14:56,757 --> 00:14:58,887
- There's always a guy like him. - Right.

424
00:14:59,157 --> 00:15:01,097
For our crew, it was Kim Seok Gu.

425
00:15:01,997 --> 00:15:04,066
I was the youngest for a long time when I served in the military.

426
00:15:04,067 --> 00:15:06,796
- Really? - I bet his seniors loved him.

427
00:15:06,797 --> 00:15:08,596
- Totally. - Yes, I agree.

428
00:15:08,597 --> 00:15:09,917
Did you have fun in the military?

429
00:15:10,537 --> 00:15:12,106
- I don't think he did. - There are so many things...

430
00:15:12,107 --> 00:15:13,707
- I can't share on TV. - Right.

431
00:15:13,877 --> 00:15:15,136
You know what? Listen.

432
00:15:15,137 --> 00:15:17,046
- He can't share them on TV. - Hey, Ji Hyeon.

433
00:15:17,047 --> 00:15:18,176
This is how I feel honestly when we talk about...

434
00:15:18,177 --> 00:15:19,417
- our military service. - Okay.

435
00:15:19,977 --> 00:15:22,417
You're not sharing your story. So I know how it must've been.

436
00:15:24,517 --> 00:15:25,986
- We can't share our story. - No.

437
00:15:25,987 --> 00:15:26,987
(I know everything.)

438
00:15:27,157 --> 00:15:28,287
Those jerks.

439
00:15:34,697 --> 00:15:36,797
I think our hiking trail is starting.

440
00:15:37,797 --> 00:15:39,867
I doubt Gi Mo works out regularly.

441
00:15:40,237 --> 00:15:41,237
I do.

442
00:15:41,797 --> 00:15:43,137
- You mean soccer? - Yes.

443
00:15:44,507 --> 00:15:47,477
Your yellow outfit makes you look like the leader.

444
00:15:47,507 --> 00:15:48,577
Right.

445
00:15:49,777 --> 00:15:51,077
It's already quite elevated.

446
00:15:52,307 --> 00:15:54,977
- This was a beautiful trail. - It's beautiful.

447
00:15:55,577 --> 00:15:56,747
How nice.

448
00:15:58,187 --> 00:15:59,717
The vibe is changing here.

449
00:16:01,887 --> 00:16:05,456
Didn't our training spot look similar to this?

450
00:16:05,457 --> 00:16:07,956
- Hey, it looked just like this. - It's starting to look legit now.

451
00:16:07,957 --> 00:16:11,297
This trail really looked similar to our training trail.

452
00:16:12,397 --> 00:16:14,137
Doesn't it feel like we're really training?

453
00:16:14,997 --> 00:16:16,806
Because I was based in Pohang,

454
00:16:16,807 --> 00:16:18,407
I barely got to see snow while I served.

455
00:16:19,007 --> 00:16:21,507
With the snow, it definitely felt different.

456
00:16:26,577 --> 00:16:29,517
(They're no longer carrying the heavy military gear.)

457
00:16:30,317 --> 00:16:32,237
(But like the day they met for the first time, )

458
00:16:32,757 --> 00:16:33,786
(they hike in their combat boots during winter.)

459
00:16:33,787 --> 00:16:35,157
Our combat boots are the best.

460
00:16:35,217 --> 00:16:36,427
- Seriously. - Yes.

461
00:16:37,127 --> 00:16:38,757
They look so cute hiking together.

462
00:16:39,427 --> 00:16:41,926
They all must be in shape since they used to be Marines.

463
00:16:41,927 --> 00:16:45,497
It just shows that all of us are tenacious by nature.

464
00:16:48,137 --> 00:16:50,067
Chang Eon. Give me the bag. I'll carry it now.

465
00:16:50,907 --> 00:16:53,607
I see. You guys are taking turns to carry the heavy backpack.

466
00:16:53,707 --> 00:16:55,236
We decided to take turns.

467
00:16:55,237 --> 00:16:56,646
But our seniors set an example.

468
00:16:56,647 --> 00:16:58,506
The one in the highest rank...

469
00:16:58,507 --> 00:17:00,147
- decided to carry it 1st. - He went 1st.

470
00:17:00,177 --> 00:17:02,847
The one in the second-highest rank decided to go next.

471
00:17:03,517 --> 00:17:05,046
It must have weighed at least 10kg.

472
00:17:05,047 --> 00:17:06,086
It went over 10kg.

473
00:17:06,087 --> 00:17:09,387
To be honest, it was fairly heavy. I was quite surprised.

474
00:17:10,527 --> 00:17:12,257
- Let me know when it gets heavy. - Yes?

475
00:17:12,357 --> 00:17:14,397
- I'm good. - My gosh.

476
00:17:16,097 --> 00:17:17,827
- Gosh, the wind. - It's getting windier.

477
00:17:18,497 --> 00:17:20,236
What time was it?

478
00:17:20,237 --> 00:17:22,067
It was around 10:30am or 11am.

479
00:17:24,237 --> 00:17:25,307
What's this?

480
00:17:26,537 --> 00:17:27,777
Hey, look at this place.

481
00:17:28,777 --> 00:17:30,176
- This might be a scenic spot. - My gosh.

482
00:17:30,177 --> 00:17:31,406
- Oh, my. - Is that Gangneung?

483
00:17:31,407 --> 00:17:33,047
My goodness.

484
00:17:33,247 --> 00:17:35,816
(They arrive at the observatory in 30 minutes without breaks.)

485
00:17:35,817 --> 00:17:37,247
It looked like CGI.

486
00:17:39,657 --> 00:17:41,187
That was the ocean.

487
00:17:42,757 --> 00:17:46,257
(Over the clouds and mountains, they see...)

488
00:17:47,197 --> 00:17:48,996
My gosh. I can see the East Sea.

489
00:17:48,997 --> 00:17:50,796
(the East Sea with blue waves.)

490
00:17:50,797 --> 00:17:52,637
- This place looks beautiful. - How beautiful.

491
00:17:53,397 --> 00:17:55,566
Look at the clouds moving. It's like a mirage.

492
00:17:55,567 --> 00:17:57,336
(The clouds look unrealistic like CGI.)

493
00:17:57,337 --> 00:17:58,606
The clouds look beautiful.

494
00:17:58,607 --> 00:17:59,937
The sky looked beautiful too.

495
00:18:00,077 --> 00:18:01,406
This place is crazy.

496
00:18:01,407 --> 00:18:04,007
(It's so beautiful.)

497
00:18:05,607 --> 00:18:08,217
This is nice. We ought to remember this view.

498
00:18:08,817 --> 00:18:10,017
This place looks amazing.

499
00:18:10,247 --> 00:18:11,447
I agree.

500
00:18:11,587 --> 00:18:13,056
The view here is amazing...

501
00:18:13,057 --> 00:18:14,287
at the top here.

502
00:18:14,657 --> 00:18:15,856
The altitude is quite high.

503
00:18:15,857 --> 00:18:17,057
Okay.

504
00:18:18,027 --> 00:18:21,096
We still have a bit more to go. I think we have 2.5km to go.

505
00:18:21,097 --> 00:18:22,257
Let's finish it.

506
00:18:23,027 --> 00:18:24,366
That looks like the perfect spot to stop.

507
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:26,266
Gosh, we were just getting started.

508
00:18:26,267 --> 00:18:27,547
We were only at a halfway point.

509
00:18:28,637 --> 00:18:33,337
(The invincible Marines keep hiking without a sip of water.)

510
00:18:35,477 --> 00:18:36,547
I'm hungry.

511
00:18:36,807 --> 00:18:38,007
I'm starting to get hungry.

512
00:18:40,247 --> 00:18:44,487
(The invincible Marine won't allow them to be weak even for a moment.)

513
00:18:44,647 --> 00:18:47,587
You look so fresh even after an hour of hiking.

514
00:18:48,757 --> 00:18:50,827
(With MINHO looking perfectly fine at the front, )

515
00:18:51,427 --> 00:18:54,027
(the other Marines don't seem tired.)

516
00:18:54,697 --> 00:18:55,997
(Panting)

517
00:18:56,727 --> 00:19:00,137
(Breathing heavily)

518
00:19:01,297 --> 00:19:04,006
(Marine Lee Gi Mo is getting out of breath.)

519
00:19:04,007 --> 00:19:05,637
(Oh, no)

520
00:19:08,207 --> 00:19:10,687
- I didn't know it was a dialect. - Me neither. I didn't know.

521
00:19:11,747 --> 00:19:13,347
- Are you tired, Gi Mo? - No, sir.

522
00:19:13,577 --> 00:19:15,277
- Everything's good. - Yes, sir!

523
00:19:16,287 --> 00:19:17,687
(My dear Gi Mo)

524
00:19:19,517 --> 00:19:21,857
You're not picking on each other for getting tired.

525
00:19:23,057 --> 00:19:24,956
Gosh, it's crazy windy today!

526
00:19:24,957 --> 00:19:26,797
- It's so windy. - It was crazy that day.

527
00:19:27,797 --> 00:19:29,226
- Give it to me now. - I'm good.

528
00:19:29,227 --> 00:19:30,297
Give it to me.

529
00:19:31,297 --> 00:19:32,996
- Give me your bag then. - I'm good.

530
00:19:32,997 --> 00:19:34,673
- Let's go. - You'll put it on top of yours?

531
00:19:34,697 --> 00:19:37,136
Hey, this must've been heavy.

532
00:19:37,137 --> 00:19:39,707
(He takes the backpack for them to share the burden.)

533
00:19:40,677 --> 00:19:42,206
Tae Hwan, this is heavy.

534
00:19:42,207 --> 00:19:44,377
My gosh. My body feels light now.

535
00:19:45,377 --> 00:19:48,517
The determination to complete the task without giving up.

536
00:19:48,977 --> 00:19:50,317
That's the spirit of Marines.

537
00:19:51,387 --> 00:19:53,817
Hold on. The lady's backpack seems heavier.

538
00:19:54,917 --> 00:19:57,527
- Forget about these Marines. - Right.

539
00:19:57,687 --> 00:19:59,757
She's even carrying her dog.

540
00:20:00,527 --> 00:20:01,756
Hey. You know?

541
00:20:01,757 --> 00:20:02,766
- This is... - She's more hardcore...

542
00:20:02,767 --> 00:20:03,797
- than you. - Hey.

543
00:20:03,927 --> 00:20:06,337
You Marines need to stop bragging. You can't even beat moms.

544
00:20:06,697 --> 00:20:07,966
- They carry so many bags of food... - Right.

545
00:20:07,967 --> 00:20:10,236
- while talking on the phone. - The timing was crazy.

546
00:20:10,237 --> 00:20:11,566
Look how comfortable the dog looks.

547
00:20:11,567 --> 00:20:13,436
- It means she's steady as a rock. - That's right.

548
00:20:13,437 --> 00:20:15,176
I bet the dog can even fall asleep since it's so comfy.

549
00:20:15,177 --> 00:20:16,706
- Hey, this is crazy. - You guys are losing your touch.

550
00:20:16,707 --> 00:20:18,247
It's the photo of the year.

551
00:20:18,477 --> 00:20:20,076
Mothers beat the spirit of Marines.

552
00:20:20,077 --> 00:20:21,117
Right.

553
00:20:21,847 --> 00:20:24,286
- Hey, is that the place? - Yes, that's the peak.

554
00:20:24,287 --> 00:20:26,007
(They only have 0.4km left until the peak.)

555
00:20:26,687 --> 00:20:27,917
Gi Mo, how about a run?

556
00:20:28,317 --> 00:20:29,357
I'll run.

557
00:20:29,657 --> 00:20:30,757
Okay.

558
00:20:31,457 --> 00:20:34,297
Run! Go!

559
00:20:34,627 --> 00:20:35,797
- One, two. - Let's go.

560
00:20:36,397 --> 00:20:39,226
- Left foot. - "Left foot."

561
00:20:39,227 --> 00:20:41,036
Left foot.

562
00:20:41,037 --> 00:20:42,496
I wonder why whenever four men get together,

563
00:20:42,497 --> 00:20:44,417
they always end up doing stupid stuff like that.

564
00:20:44,937 --> 00:20:47,377
- One, two, three, four. One, two. - One, two.

565
00:20:47,907 --> 00:20:49,037
- One, two. - One, two.

566
00:20:49,447 --> 00:20:52,277
- One, two, three, four. One, two. - One, two.

567
00:20:52,677 --> 00:20:54,316
- One, two. Let's beat this. - One, two.

568
00:20:54,317 --> 00:20:56,616
- One, two, three, four. One, two. - Stop it.

569
00:20:56,617 --> 00:20:58,417
(As MINHO tenaciously keeps on counting, )

570
00:20:58,887 --> 00:20:59,887
(his comrades try to keep up.)

571
00:20:59,888 --> 00:21:01,717
- They can keep up with you. - One, two.

572
00:21:01,857 --> 00:21:04,057
Invincible Marines, shout it out. Go!

573
00:21:04,357 --> 00:21:05,887
- Invincible. - Invincible.

574
00:21:06,557 --> 00:21:07,597
- Marines. - Marines.

575
00:21:08,197 --> 00:21:10,467
- Invincible Marines. - Invincible Marines.

576
00:21:11,197 --> 00:21:14,237
- Marines, always victorious. - Marines, always victorious.

577
00:21:14,337 --> 00:21:17,667
- Ghost-catching Marines! - Ghost-catching Marines!

578
00:21:17,737 --> 00:21:19,906
- Gosh, we're almost there. - Let's go.

579
00:21:19,907 --> 00:21:20,976
(Amazed)

580
00:21:20,977 --> 00:21:22,206
We're almost there.

581
00:21:22,207 --> 00:21:24,747
(They're so close to the peak.)

582
00:21:26,147 --> 00:21:28,116
(They finish half of the trail in 1 hour and 20 minutes.)

583
00:21:28,117 --> 00:21:29,816
You got there in 1 hour and 20 minutes.

584
00:21:29,817 --> 00:21:30,946
Isn't that really fast?

585
00:21:30,947 --> 00:21:32,517
Right. They're not on flat surface.

586
00:21:32,817 --> 00:21:34,187
This place is huge.

587
00:21:34,887 --> 00:21:36,826
(Out of breath)

588
00:21:36,827 --> 00:21:38,957
(Oh, no. Poor Gi Mo.)

589
00:21:39,897 --> 00:21:40,996
That was a crazy workout.

590
00:21:40,997 --> 00:21:42,926
(We came, saw, and beat it.)

591
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:44,767
Gosh, that was a nice way to end it.

592
00:21:45,167 --> 00:21:46,396
- You must be tired. - Good work.

593
00:21:46,397 --> 00:21:48,697
(Baekdudaegan Seonjaryeong)

594
00:21:49,937 --> 00:21:51,577
(Taking a picture to remember the moment)

595
00:21:52,507 --> 00:21:54,207
We came all the way here to see this.

596
00:21:55,577 --> 00:21:57,277
I felt proud.

597
00:21:57,477 --> 00:22:00,876
We ran up toward the end.

598
00:22:00,877 --> 00:22:03,516
Racing to the peak was the right call.

599
00:22:03,517 --> 00:22:05,047
It made the trail even more rewarding.

600
00:22:05,587 --> 00:22:07,116
It was quite windy,

601
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,356
but we didn't have to carry firearms.

602
00:22:08,357 --> 00:22:10,237
We weren't wearing bullet-proof helmets either.

603
00:22:10,857 --> 00:22:12,757
I felt so light without my gear.

604
00:22:12,827 --> 00:22:14,657
This was a piece of cake for us.

605
00:22:15,697 --> 00:22:16,927
I mean it.

606
00:22:18,727 --> 00:22:19,766
One, two.

607
00:22:19,767 --> 00:22:21,036
(They all take a selfie together.)

608
00:22:21,037 --> 00:22:22,067
Okay.

609
00:22:23,867 --> 00:22:25,736
That was neat.

610
00:22:25,737 --> 00:22:27,083
(We did a neat job like true invincible Marines.)

611
00:22:27,107 --> 00:22:28,336
Gosh, it's cold.

612
00:22:28,337 --> 00:22:29,677
This place has a nice vibe.

613
00:22:31,147 --> 00:22:32,746
Let's eat it on the ground. We can just elevate it.

614
00:22:32,747 --> 00:22:34,346
Gosh, it must've been so cold...

615
00:22:34,347 --> 00:22:35,917
- up there. - Yes.

616
00:22:35,947 --> 00:22:37,616
Eating ramyeon at the top is different, though.

617
00:22:37,617 --> 00:22:38,617
(Chuckling)

618
00:22:39,147 --> 00:22:41,157
- Set it up. - I'll set it up.

619
00:22:41,717 --> 00:22:43,887
- Gosh, I'm starving. - It looks so good.

620
00:22:44,987 --> 00:22:47,527
(Everyone busily shakes their seasoning packet.)

621
00:22:48,097 --> 00:22:50,196
We carry this heavy backpack for this, right?

622
00:22:50,197 --> 00:22:51,496
That's right.

623
00:22:51,497 --> 00:22:54,266
- I can't see. - A little bit more. Great.

624
00:22:54,267 --> 00:22:55,796
(Pouring the steaming hot water)

625
00:22:55,797 --> 00:22:56,907
It's warm.

626
00:22:57,037 --> 00:22:58,167
I'm good.

627
00:22:58,437 --> 00:22:59,476
Stop.

628
00:22:59,477 --> 00:23:01,036
(Filling up their bowl in order)

629
00:23:01,037 --> 00:23:02,576
- Everyone got their favorite. - That's good.

630
00:23:02,577 --> 00:23:03,947
We got our favorite.

631
00:23:04,307 --> 00:23:06,046
(Rummaging through)

632
00:23:06,047 --> 00:23:07,177
Did you pack more food?

633
00:23:09,717 --> 00:23:11,547
You can't have ramyeon without gimbap.

634
00:23:12,417 --> 00:23:13,657
- What? - Gimbap.

635
00:23:14,257 --> 00:23:15,356
Gimbap.

636
00:23:15,357 --> 00:23:16,486
(Surprised)

637
00:23:16,487 --> 00:23:18,226
I didn't know. But we had gimbap in the backpack.

638
00:23:18,227 --> 00:23:20,727
- That's why it was heavy. - I bet the gimbap was heavy.

639
00:23:21,527 --> 00:23:22,656
When did you pack this?

640
00:23:22,657 --> 00:23:24,267
I got it this morning.

641
00:23:24,967 --> 00:23:26,867
- You're well-disciplined. - Thank you, sir!

642
00:23:27,297 --> 00:23:28,367
"Thank you, sir!"

643
00:23:30,207 --> 00:23:31,537
I bought cheese and tuna gimbap.

644
00:23:32,337 --> 00:23:33,407
- Gosh. - Okay.

645
00:23:34,677 --> 00:23:36,546
(The table is filled with ramyeon and gimbap.)

646
00:23:36,547 --> 00:23:37,577
They look good.

647
00:23:38,747 --> 00:23:40,677
- Gosh, that does look good. - Right.

648
00:23:42,017 --> 00:23:43,387
Should I have the gimbap first?

649
00:23:47,617 --> 00:23:48,716
I bet it's good.

650
00:23:48,717 --> 00:23:50,357
Gimbap is tasty when you eat it outdoors.

651
00:23:50,657 --> 00:23:51,757
I want the tuna gimbap.

652
00:23:57,697 --> 00:23:58,927
It's so good.

653
00:23:59,867 --> 00:24:01,296
- I'm just sitting on the ground. - Gosh, that looks good.

654
00:24:01,297 --> 00:24:02,597
- That looks so good. - My gosh.

655
00:24:02,907 --> 00:24:04,206
Eat when the noodles are firm.

656
00:24:04,207 --> 00:24:08,307
(Quickly slurping the noodles when they're still firm)

657
00:24:10,307 --> 00:24:11,347
My gosh.

658
00:24:12,307 --> 00:24:14,817
(This is what I'm talking about.)

659
00:24:15,677 --> 00:24:17,587
This is a universal truth about ramyeon.

660
00:24:18,187 --> 00:24:20,587
Ramyeon after a long day tastes the best.

661
00:24:20,787 --> 00:24:21,887
I agree.

662
00:24:22,217 --> 00:24:23,426
It was so good.

663
00:24:23,427 --> 00:24:24,987
- It was really good. - Seriously.

664
00:24:25,927 --> 00:24:27,757
(The unforgettable flavor...)

665
00:24:29,297 --> 00:24:31,827
(after a hard day of training)

666
00:24:33,837 --> 00:24:35,796
- Oddly, it tastes good outdoors. - Right.

667
00:24:35,797 --> 00:24:37,137
- Right? - It's odd.

668
00:24:37,307 --> 00:24:39,367
- It's better on a cold day too. - Right.

669
00:24:39,467 --> 00:24:41,506
You need to sweat a bit after a good workout.

670
00:24:41,507 --> 00:24:43,707
- Right. - It makes ramyeon tastier.

671
00:24:45,447 --> 00:24:48,116
(The Marines gobble up the ramyeon.)

672
00:24:48,117 --> 00:24:49,416
They must've been quite tired.

673
00:24:49,417 --> 00:24:51,287
They must be happiest at that moment.

674
00:24:52,247 --> 00:24:53,686
- Gi Mo, you know DELD, right? - Yes.

675
00:24:53,687 --> 00:24:55,356
- DELD. - DELD.

676
00:24:55,357 --> 00:24:57,287
DELD? Is it drink every last drop?

677
00:24:57,427 --> 00:24:58,957
You must drink every last drop.

678
00:25:02,357 --> 00:25:05,167
(Slurping the noodles first)

679
00:25:06,167 --> 00:25:08,537
(Gulping it down)

680
00:25:09,867 --> 00:25:12,167
(Hitting the spot)

681
00:25:12,977 --> 00:25:15,536
(He drinks every last drop of it in an instant.)

682
00:25:15,537 --> 00:25:16,547
(Feeling proud)

683
00:25:20,277 --> 00:25:21,916
Let's clean this up.

684
00:25:21,917 --> 00:25:23,517
(They clean up the spot where they ate.)

685
00:25:23,787 --> 00:25:25,447
You know what? We came all the way here.

686
00:25:25,947 --> 00:25:27,756
- We should take a picture. - Yes.

687
00:25:27,757 --> 00:25:29,517
- Did you get it ready? - I'll get it ready.

688
00:25:29,757 --> 00:25:31,317
We'll go shirtless if we don't have it.

689
00:25:31,487 --> 00:25:32,727
(Go shirtless?)

690
00:25:33,797 --> 00:25:35,557
(He takes off his jacket to take a picture.)

691
00:25:36,897 --> 00:25:38,996
(What's going on?)

692
00:25:38,997 --> 00:25:40,697
(A knowing smile)

693
00:25:40,930 --> 00:25:42,070
I'll get it ready.

694
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,960
We'll go shirtless if we don't have it.

695
00:25:45,140 --> 00:25:46,770
- Let's take one and go. - Get ready.

696
00:25:48,210 --> 00:25:50,679
I haven't worn this in a while. It's been five years.

697
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,709
(Marine Corp)

698
00:25:51,710 --> 00:25:54,980
(Sighing)

699
00:25:56,250 --> 00:25:58,579
(They transform into true Marines.)

700
00:25:58,580 --> 00:25:59,620
Seriously.

701
00:26:01,290 --> 00:26:03,289
That was my idea.

702
00:26:03,290 --> 00:26:04,320
Really?

703
00:26:05,060 --> 00:26:07,790
It might offend some people when I say this.

704
00:26:08,090 --> 00:26:09,729
All the military uniforms have the same digital camouflage pattern.

705
00:26:09,730 --> 00:26:11,659
But the Marine uniform looks the best. I'm serious.

706
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:14,300
(But the Marine uniform looks the best. I'm serious.)

707
00:26:14,730 --> 00:26:16,199
- My gosh. - Sure. I can see that.

708
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,499
- I'm serious. - I agree.

709
00:26:17,500 --> 00:26:18,999
- I'm serious. - Sure.

710
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,910
Our uniform looks so much better.

711
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:22,309
I'm sorry to interrupt.

712
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:23,956
But we don't consider uniforms with that pattern authentic.

713
00:26:23,980 --> 00:26:25,479
- What? - That's not a real uniform.

714
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:26,679
(The old-school ones are real.)

715
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:28,120
- What? - That's not a real uniform.

716
00:26:29,180 --> 00:26:32,480
Hey. We didn't think highly of the Army uniform.

717
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:34,790
The Army uniform didn't look sharp.

718
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,919
The combat uniform conscripted police wear...

719
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,589
- Hey, don't be ridiculous. - looks really sharp.

720
00:26:39,590 --> 00:26:40,659
Come on.

721
00:26:40,660 --> 00:26:43,199
You just crossed the line. I'm serious.

722
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:45,899
- I swear. Our uniform is the best. - Hey.

723
00:26:45,900 --> 00:26:47,670
Hey, that's not a real uniform.

724
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:48,999
We used to wear combat uniforms.

725
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,599
- I mean, field uniforms. - I see. Field uniforms.

726
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:51,769
They look great when worn properly.

727
00:26:51,770 --> 00:26:53,869
But the Army uniforms don't look that cool.

728
00:26:53,870 --> 00:26:55,439
The US military has the best uniforms.

729
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:56,479
(Do you know KATUSA?)

730
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,609
What are you talking about?

731
00:26:57,610 --> 00:26:59,486
- Anyway, the old-school... - Haven't you seen the movie?

732
00:26:59,510 --> 00:27:01,049
- The old-school one... - Haven't you seen it?

733
00:27:01,050 --> 00:27:02,179
Looked weird and tacky.

734
00:27:02,180 --> 00:27:04,260
Haven't you watched the move, "Saving Private Ryan?"

735
00:27:04,950 --> 00:27:06,549
- Stand in front of that. - In front of that?

736
00:27:06,550 --> 00:27:08,490
(The group dresses in red to take a picture.)

737
00:27:09,290 --> 00:27:10,960
- All good? - Look over there.

738
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:13,829
Gi Mo's shirt got too small for him.

739
00:27:13,830 --> 00:27:15,030
I thought he was Wilson.

740
00:27:16,090 --> 00:27:17,650
- Red Wilson. - Wilson with a shirt on.

741
00:27:17,860 --> 00:27:19,130
He's Red Wilson.

742
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:22,200
- Gosh, it's cold. - He's just so adorable.

743
00:27:22,870 --> 00:27:25,470
Should I take off this jacket?

744
00:27:25,940 --> 00:27:27,709
- Keep it on. That's better. - Keep it on.

745
00:27:27,710 --> 00:27:29,409
- That's better than the sweater. - Okay.

746
00:27:29,410 --> 00:27:32,480
(He wears the padded jacket instead of going shirtless.)

747
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:35,550
Ten, nine, eight, seven...

748
00:27:35,910 --> 00:27:38,350
- Four, three, two. - Okay.

749
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,790
(Looking disciplined right away)

750
00:27:41,620 --> 00:27:43,389
(We're the Marines.)

751
00:27:43,390 --> 00:27:45,270
The uniform makes everyone behave the same way.

752
00:27:45,620 --> 00:27:46,690
Okay.

753
00:27:46,990 --> 00:27:48,230
Turn around.

754
00:27:49,130 --> 00:27:50,529
(Turn around!)

755
00:27:50,530 --> 00:27:51,730
We look like sausages.

756
00:27:52,130 --> 00:27:53,970
- Six, five, - What kind of pose should we do?

757
00:27:54,130 --> 00:27:55,730
- four... - Should we do this?

758
00:27:59,300 --> 00:28:00,309
(Cringing)

759
00:28:00,310 --> 00:28:02,539
(A ghost wouldn't even dare to come close at this vibe.)

760
00:28:02,540 --> 00:28:04,440
We probably got it, right? Gosh, it's cold.

761
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:07,179
Okay.

762
00:28:07,180 --> 00:28:08,310
(Grabbing)

763
00:28:09,150 --> 00:28:11,720
(Look at this.)

764
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:14,189
(They conquer mountains after the sea.)

765
00:28:14,190 --> 00:28:15,419
- Gosh, that's funny. - Okay.

766
00:28:15,420 --> 00:28:16,690
That's a nice picture.

767
00:28:17,560 --> 00:28:20,690
(They pack up after making a special memory.)

768
00:28:20,930 --> 00:28:22,430
Let's go down with good energy.

769
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:24,400
Let's go.

770
00:28:24,930 --> 00:28:28,300
Baekdudaegan Seonjaryeong, bye.

771
00:28:28,770 --> 00:28:29,830
Bye.

772
00:28:31,170 --> 00:28:32,469
Going down is easy.

773
00:28:32,470 --> 00:28:33,910
(Baekdudaegan)

