(He makes his bed as he checks the time in the morning.)

1293
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:27,100
(Clean)

1294
00:47:27,440 --> 00:47:29,070
Let's eat first.

1295
00:47:31,040 --> 00:47:33,479
I'll make egg rice.

1296
00:47:33,480 --> 00:47:35,560
(He'll eat a simple meal of the soy sauce egg rice.)

1297
00:47:37,280 --> 00:47:39,720
(He pours oil into the hot pan.)

1298
00:47:39,920 --> 00:47:41,090
(Cracking)

1299
00:47:42,190 --> 00:47:44,590
(He cracks open an egg and drops it into the pan.)

1300
00:47:46,820 --> 00:47:48,060
There are two yolks.

1301
00:47:48,760 --> 00:47:50,389
- There are two yolks. - Two yolks.

1302
00:47:50,390 --> 00:47:52,430
- It feels good. - That's right. It feels good.

1303
00:47:54,260 --> 00:47:55,569
I'm off to a good start.

1304
00:47:55,570 --> 00:47:56,870
(I got lucky.)

1305
00:47:57,970 --> 00:47:59,640
(Cutting)

1306
00:48:00,340 --> 00:48:01,969
(He slices chili peppers on the kitchen counter.)

1307
00:48:01,970 --> 00:48:03,870
(Fascinated)

1308
00:48:04,040 --> 00:48:05,339
Let's make it spicy.

1309
00:48:05,340 --> 00:48:07,080
(He adds spiciness.)

1310
00:48:07,710 --> 00:48:10,280
(He pours a bit of soy sauce over the double-yolk egg.)

1311
00:48:10,710 --> 00:48:13,719
Why do you pour soy sauce directly over the egg?

1312
00:48:13,720 --> 00:48:15,119
That's my secret.

1313
00:48:15,120 --> 00:48:16,289
- Really? - The burnt soy sauce...

1314
00:48:16,290 --> 00:48:18,820
gives it a smoky flavor.

1315
00:48:19,190 --> 00:48:21,930
It's much tastier to add that to rice.

1316
00:48:22,090 --> 00:48:23,489
- It's for a smoky flavor. - Yes.

1317
00:48:23,490 --> 00:48:24,859
Good.

1318
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:26,659
(The simple dish of soy sauce egg rice is complete.)

1319
00:48:26,660 --> 00:48:28,530
- That's how you eat it. - It looks tasty.

1320
00:48:31,100 --> 00:48:32,239
Let's make it spicy.

1321
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:33,500
(Wiping)

1322
00:48:34,200 --> 00:48:35,639
He eats like Hyun Moo.

1323
00:48:35,640 --> 00:48:36,810
You eat standing up.

1324
00:48:37,440 --> 00:48:39,439
I've begun to do that. It feels good.

1325
00:48:39,440 --> 00:48:40,910
I guess I made it trendy.

1326
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:44,680
You think the world revolves around you, Hyun Moo.

1327
00:48:45,620 --> 00:48:47,380
(Moo-centric theory is the truth!)

1328
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:50,050
(He joins on the trend without even realizing it.)

1329
00:48:50,750 --> 00:48:52,260
It smells so tasty.

1330
00:48:54,020 --> 00:48:56,260
It's really tasty with chili pepper.

1331
00:48:58,560 --> 00:49:00,500
(Halting)

1332
00:49:01,970 --> 00:49:03,370
Did she leave her phone on the bus?

1333
00:49:03,430 --> 00:49:04,499
(He calls someone in the middle of mixing the rice.)

1334
00:49:04,500 --> 00:49:05,540
Did she leave it at home?

1335
00:49:07,870 --> 00:49:09,470
- My baby. - Mom.

1336
00:49:09,570 --> 00:49:11,210
What? I see.

1337
00:49:11,910 --> 00:49:13,780
- Hey. - At what time will you arrive?

1338
00:49:15,010 --> 00:49:17,249
It said that it'd take 2 hours and 20 minutes.

1339
00:49:17,250 --> 00:49:18,610
You got on the bus at 10am, right?

1340
00:49:18,820 --> 00:49:20,319
Yes. I set off at 10am.

1341
00:49:20,320 --> 00:49:21,450
Okay.

1342
00:49:21,520 --> 00:49:23,149
- I love you. - Okay.

1343
00:49:23,150 --> 00:49:24,350
Gosh, ma'am.

1344
00:49:25,990 --> 00:49:29,030
My mom hasn't come to my place in a long while.

1345
00:49:29,130 --> 00:49:30,829
So she decided...

1346
00:49:30,830 --> 00:49:33,259
to come to my place for the first time in a while...

1347
00:49:33,260 --> 00:49:35,699
and see if I was living well.

1348
00:49:35,700 --> 00:49:37,100
(It's the day his mom is visiting.)

1349
00:49:37,130 --> 00:49:40,240
To park my car at the bus terminal...

1350
00:49:40,370 --> 00:49:42,310
and pick my mom up,

1351
00:49:42,440 --> 00:49:44,269
I needed 40 to 50 minutes.

1352
00:49:44,270 --> 00:49:46,239
That meant I needed to leave the house by 11:30am.

1353
00:49:46,240 --> 00:49:49,849
To avoid her nagging... I mean, to avoid her advice,

1354
00:49:49,850 --> 00:49:51,149
I needed to clean the house.

1355
00:49:51,150 --> 00:49:53,320
So I didn't have time to eat at the table.

1356
00:49:53,420 --> 00:49:56,150
That was why I ate quickly while standing up.

1357
00:49:56,690 --> 00:49:58,360
That was why you ate while standing up.

1358
00:49:58,460 --> 00:50:00,489
- You didn't have time. - You need to work fast.

1359
00:50:00,490 --> 00:50:02,859
If you don't clean up, your mom does it.

1360
00:50:02,860 --> 00:50:05,459
Yes. Then my belongings disappear.

1361
00:50:05,460 --> 00:50:07,430
That isn't the issue. It's hard on your mom.

1362
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:09,630
It's hard on my mom.

1363
00:50:09,670 --> 00:50:11,969
Whenever my mom visits, my belongings disappear.

1364
00:50:11,970 --> 00:50:14,099
- I know how you feel. - Of course.

1365
00:50:14,100 --> 00:50:16,039
Your mom cherished you and raised you well.

1366
00:50:16,040 --> 00:50:19,139
Do announcers tend to be unfilial?

1367
00:50:19,140 --> 00:50:21,009
- That's the criterion. - Is that the criterion?

1368
00:50:21,010 --> 00:50:23,809
Yes. The first criterion of being an announcer is...

1369
00:50:23,810 --> 00:50:25,096
- the lack of filial piety. - The lack of filial piety.

1370
00:50:25,120 --> 00:50:26,819
Is that a part of the test?

1371
00:50:26,820 --> 00:50:28,749
- Yes. It's a part of the interview. - Is there a score...

1372
00:50:28,750 --> 00:50:30,270
- for the lack of filial piety? - Yes.

1373
00:50:30,820 --> 00:50:32,459
(The Lack of Filial Piety)

1374
00:50:32,460 --> 00:50:33,559
(1. What do you do when you need to barp during a call with Mom?)

1375
00:50:33,560 --> 00:50:34,590
(Don't hold it in.)

1376
00:50:35,290 --> 00:50:37,129
(2. Whose duty is handwashing my clothes?)

1377
00:50:37,130 --> 00:50:39,059
(My mom's duty)

1378
00:50:39,060 --> 00:50:41,800
(He gets a high score when it comes to the lack of filial piety.)

1379
00:50:42,070 --> 00:50:43,770
Only the announcers understand.

1380
00:50:43,900 --> 00:50:45,369
It's the world of announcers.

1381
00:50:45,370 --> 00:50:46,370
(It's a virtue for us.)

1382
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,269
(He'll be filial today since his mom is visiting.)

1383
00:50:48,270 --> 00:50:49,740
(Eating)

1384
00:50:51,840 --> 00:50:53,410
(Humming in approval)

1385
00:50:54,010 --> 00:50:55,779
(There's no relaxation...)

1386
00:50:55,780 --> 00:50:57,210
(he showed last time.)

1387
00:50:58,050 --> 00:50:59,820
(Eating hurriedly)

1388
00:51:00,550 --> 00:51:02,790
He's shoving in food since he needs to eat fast.

1389
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:07,090
(Eating)

1390
00:51:08,660 --> 00:51:11,230
(He quickly finishes eating while standing up.)

1391
00:51:14,430 --> 00:51:17,830
(He quickly does the dishes.)

1392
00:51:18,800 --> 00:51:19,870
What time is it now?

1393
00:51:22,240 --> 00:51:25,210
It's 11am. I'm a bit behind.

1394
00:51:25,610 --> 00:51:27,239
I need to clean the house quickly.

1395
00:51:27,240 --> 00:51:29,000
(He needs to finish cleaning in 30 minutes.)

1396
00:51:29,510 --> 00:51:31,150
The veranda is in a terrible state.

1397
00:51:31,920 --> 00:51:34,119
There's a lot to clean up.

1398
00:51:34,120 --> 00:51:35,749
You don't have enough time.

1399
00:51:35,750 --> 00:51:37,889
I bet your mom will say, "Why is the veranda so messy?"

1400
00:51:37,890 --> 00:51:39,990
- My goodness. That won't do. - I'm sure of it.

1401
00:51:40,560 --> 00:51:42,490
"Do you live alone to be so messy?"

1402
00:51:43,630 --> 00:51:44,930
I think she'll say something.

1403
00:51:46,160 --> 00:51:47,900
(This won't do.)

1404
00:51:49,200 --> 00:51:50,200
What's that?

1405
00:51:50,201 --> 00:51:51,740
(He pulls a canopy over it.)

1406
00:51:53,700 --> 00:51:55,609
He pulled a canopy over it.

1407
00:51:55,610 --> 00:51:57,570
I hid it under the cloth.

1408
00:51:59,340 --> 00:52:02,680
It's okay. I can do it.

1409
00:52:04,720 --> 00:52:06,720
Let's put them inside.

1410
00:52:07,380 --> 00:52:08,449
It's like cleaning the barracks.

1411
00:52:08,450 --> 00:52:09,950
He seems like a soldier.

1412
00:52:11,620 --> 00:52:13,759
(He spins the container to keep it out of his mom's sight.)

1413
00:52:13,760 --> 00:52:16,130
You spun it to keep it out of her sight.

1414
00:52:18,260 --> 00:52:20,229
(Let's see.)

1415
00:52:20,230 --> 00:52:21,500
Let's put it here.

1416
00:52:22,070 --> 00:52:23,600
It'll hide the stove.

1417
00:52:24,130 --> 00:52:25,640
He's hiding everything.

1418
00:52:26,740 --> 00:52:27,939
All right.

1419
00:52:27,940 --> 00:52:29,810
(He displays cool items.)

1420
00:52:30,040 --> 00:52:32,310
I'll display it so that my mom can see it.

1421
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:33,680
The autographed T-shirt.

1422
00:52:33,681 --> 00:52:35,850
I interviewed Heo Hoon.

1423
00:52:36,750 --> 00:52:38,750
I need to make her happy.

1424
00:52:39,950 --> 00:52:41,180
What time is it now?

1425
00:52:42,650 --> 00:52:43,719
(It's already 11:15am.)

1426
00:52:43,720 --> 00:52:45,360
Don't you need to get ready and head out?

1427
00:52:46,720 --> 00:52:48,490
(To avoid his mom's advice, )

1428
00:52:49,260 --> 00:52:50,329
All right.

1429
00:52:50,330 --> 00:52:52,230
(he needs to clean up as much as he can!)

1430
00:52:52,560 --> 00:52:54,059
Time passes quickly when you clean up.

1431
00:52:54,060 --> 00:52:55,100
That's right.

1432
00:52:55,370 --> 00:52:56,799
Let's change it.

1433
00:52:56,800 --> 00:52:59,600
(He works fast to hide the dirty parts of the house.)

1434
00:53:01,610 --> 00:53:02,670
What time is it now?

1435
00:53:03,040 --> 00:53:04,340
I need to head out.

1436
00:53:06,080 --> 00:53:07,180
Still...

1437
00:53:08,280 --> 00:53:10,209
- The things I'm thankful for. - What?

1438
00:53:10,210 --> 00:53:11,879
- Is he writing a diary? - He still does that.

1439
00:53:11,880 --> 00:53:13,650
- Why do that when he's so busy? - I know.

1440
00:53:13,850 --> 00:53:15,320
Firstly, I'm thankful...

1441
00:53:16,790 --> 00:53:20,220
that Mom can come to Seoul in a healthy state.

1442
00:53:22,460 --> 00:53:23,980
I'm thankful that the weather is cold.

1443
00:53:24,900 --> 00:53:25,929
Good.

1444
00:53:25,930 --> 00:53:29,200
(After completing his morning routine)

1445
00:53:30,730 --> 00:53:32,670
(Adjusting)

1446
00:53:33,800 --> 00:53:36,009
Mom likes it when I wear a tie.

1447
00:53:36,010 --> 00:53:37,010
A tie.

1448
00:53:37,940 --> 00:53:39,110
Not bad.

1449
00:53:39,840 --> 00:53:41,610
- She likes it when you look neat. - Yes.

1450
00:53:42,050 --> 00:53:44,709
- When you meet your parents, - Yes.

1451
00:53:44,710 --> 00:53:46,880
It's important to wear neat clothes.

1452
00:53:47,050 --> 00:53:49,719
It's a way of showing them that you're living well.

1453
00:53:49,720 --> 00:53:50,749
That makes sense.

1454
00:53:50,750 --> 00:53:53,619
When they see their son looking neat and pretty,

1455
00:53:53,620 --> 00:53:55,360
- they feel proud. - That's right.

1456
00:53:55,530 --> 00:53:58,060
I made a lot of effort since she doesn't visit often.

1457
00:53:59,130 --> 00:54:00,359
(He puts a lot of care into getting ready.)

1458
00:54:00,360 --> 00:54:01,400
All done.

1459
00:54:02,500 --> 00:54:03,700
(Spraying)

1460
00:54:04,430 --> 00:54:06,800
(He sprays air freshener.)

1461
00:54:07,100 --> 00:54:08,580
You're putting a lot of care into it.

1462
00:54:09,910 --> 00:54:11,780
The woody fragrance will smell natural.

1463
00:54:12,880 --> 00:54:14,439
Why are you spraying so much?

1464
00:54:14,440 --> 00:54:15,986
My mom is sensitive when it comes to smell.

1465
00:54:16,010 --> 00:54:17,150
- Really? - Yes.

1466
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:20,320
(Spraying)

1467
00:54:20,950 --> 00:54:22,790
What? Aren't you spraying too much?

1468
00:54:23,450 --> 00:54:26,520
Is your mom visiting for inspection?

1469
00:54:26,660 --> 00:54:28,820
- Is she an inspector? - Will she wear white gloves...

1470
00:54:29,430 --> 00:54:30,460
and do this?

1471
00:54:31,160 --> 00:54:32,460
"Did you wipe this part?"

1472
00:54:34,200 --> 00:54:35,430
Let's go.

1473
00:54:37,300 --> 00:54:40,240
(Mom, I'm on my way.)

1474
00:54:41,370 --> 00:54:43,470
(At 11:40am, he finally sets off.)

1475
00:54:44,170 --> 00:54:45,380
The weather is nice.

1476
00:54:47,140 --> 00:54:50,210
(He heads over to the bus terminal as he listens to music.)

1477
00:54:51,520 --> 00:54:53,420
Mom likes Lee Eun Ha.

1478
00:54:55,590 --> 00:54:57,490
"You Let Me Go with a Smile."

1479
00:54:58,960 --> 00:55:00,019
(He finishes setting up the playlist.)

1480
00:55:00,020 --> 00:55:01,259
You're attentive.

1481
00:55:01,260 --> 00:55:03,489
I always play old songs.

1482
00:55:03,490 --> 00:55:05,299
- A playlist of her favorite songs. - Yes.

1483
00:55:05,300 --> 00:55:06,400
Old songs.

1484
00:55:06,960 --> 00:55:08,599
(He drives as he listens...)

1485
00:55:08,600 --> 00:55:09,970
(to his mom's favorite songs.)

1486
00:55:11,130 --> 00:55:13,840
(He sees his destination.)

1487
00:55:15,770 --> 00:55:17,410
(Glancing over)

1488
00:55:17,670 --> 00:55:20,240
It's 12:10pm. She'll be here in 15 minutes.

1489
00:55:21,710 --> 00:55:24,030
(As he checks the arrival time of the bus his mom is on, )

1490
00:55:24,810 --> 00:55:27,520
(he arrives at the bus terminal.)

1491
00:55:28,950 --> 00:55:31,690
(He fixes his clothes before meeting her.)

1492
00:55:33,160 --> 00:55:35,630
- Kang Yong, you look cool. - He looks cool.

1493
00:55:37,430 --> 00:55:38,730
It's 12:21pm. I'm late.

1494
00:55:39,400 --> 00:55:40,800
(Flustered)

1495
00:55:41,230 --> 00:55:44,330
(Feeling pressed for time, he quickens his steps.)

1496
00:55:45,370 --> 00:55:47,340
It's 12:21pm. She'll be here soon.

1497
00:55:47,570 --> 00:55:49,340
She'll be here in one minute.

1498
00:55:50,310 --> 00:55:52,790
(It's 1 minute before her arrival, so he speeds up even more.)

1499
00:55:52,940 --> 00:55:55,010
She must be here. I need to hurry up.

1500
00:55:58,850 --> 00:55:59,850
Where is she?

1501
00:56:01,020 --> 00:56:02,190
My goodness.

1502
00:56:02,890 --> 00:56:04,320
This is the gate.

1503
00:56:07,060 --> 00:56:09,790
(Chuckling)

1504
00:56:11,330 --> 00:56:13,800
I knew you'd do this.

1505
00:56:15,070 --> 00:56:17,530
She currently lives in Gunsan, North Jeolla Province.

1506
00:56:17,700 --> 00:56:18,970
She traveled a long way.

1507
00:56:19,600 --> 00:56:21,670
(In the fridge of Kang Yong who lives alone)

1508
00:56:23,040 --> 00:56:25,240
- I see. - She makes me sticky rice.

1509
00:56:27,180 --> 00:56:28,649
(I watched today's episode...)

1510
00:56:28,650 --> 00:56:30,250
(of "News Anhani," the Youtube channel.)

1511
00:56:30,780 --> 00:56:32,779
(She monitors his shows...)

1512
00:56:32,780 --> 00:56:35,120
(and gives him a thumbs up.)

1513
00:56:35,590 --> 00:56:36,990
You brought so many things.

1514
00:56:37,290 --> 00:56:39,320
Did she bring those boxes alone?

1515
00:56:39,760 --> 00:56:40,919
I tell her to bring just a little bit,

1516
00:56:40,920 --> 00:56:42,689
- but she doesn't listen. - Of course not.

1517
00:56:42,690 --> 00:56:44,059
Even when you tell her to bring just a little bit,

1518
00:56:44,060 --> 00:56:45,559
- she brings a lot. - Yes.

1519
00:56:45,560 --> 00:56:46,730
She loads the compartment.

1520
00:56:47,160 --> 00:56:48,330
- Just two. - Really?

1521
00:56:49,070 --> 00:56:51,300
They aren't very heavy. Take a hot pack.

1522
00:56:52,140 --> 00:56:53,499
It's okay.

1523
00:56:53,500 --> 00:56:55,310
Let's go.

1524
00:56:55,870 --> 00:56:57,040
Let's go.

1525
00:56:57,240 --> 00:57:00,180
Why did you bring so many things?

1526
00:57:02,250 --> 00:57:03,480
Did you have breakfast?

1527
00:57:03,650 --> 00:57:05,379
- Yes, I did. - I see.

1528
00:57:05,380 --> 00:57:06,650
I had egg rice.

1529
00:57:07,220 --> 00:57:08,420
- Egg rice? - Yes.

1530
00:57:09,290 --> 00:57:11,920
- Did you have breakfast? - I had breakfast as I always do.

1531
00:57:12,390 --> 00:57:14,560
I also had a snack on my way here.

1532
00:57:14,690 --> 00:57:15,959
- What did you eat? - What?

1533
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:17,990
- What did you eat? - The way you talk...

1534
00:57:18,730 --> 00:57:20,059
"Did you have lunch?"

1535
00:57:20,060 --> 00:57:21,769
(Homely)

1536
00:57:21,770 --> 00:57:24,570
I make an effort to be affectionate.

1537
00:57:24,900 --> 00:57:26,470
How old is your mom?

1538
00:57:26,670 --> 00:57:28,440
She was born in 1960.

1539
00:57:28,640 --> 00:57:29,739
She had me at a late age.

1540
00:57:29,740 --> 00:57:30,909
- You were born late. - I was born late.

1541
00:57:30,910 --> 00:57:32,609
She had me at the age of 36 or 37.

1542
00:57:32,610 --> 00:57:33,639
I see.

1543
00:57:33,640 --> 00:57:35,449
That's why you care about her more.

1544
00:57:35,450 --> 00:57:36,510
Yes.

1545
00:57:37,010 --> 00:57:38,380
- I had this. - Okay.

1546
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:40,150
Okay.

1547
00:57:40,620 --> 00:57:42,050
It's cold, so don't take it out.

1548
00:57:44,620 --> 00:57:46,780
Sit in the back. I'll do it, Mom. Just get in the car.

1549
00:57:47,860 --> 00:57:49,060
- Is the door open? - Yes.

1550
00:57:51,230 --> 00:57:53,130
I'll put them on the seat like this.

1551
00:57:53,900 --> 00:57:55,029
- Give me your bag. - Can I get in now?

1552
00:57:55,030 --> 00:57:56,769
- It's okay. I need to drink. - Really?

1553
00:57:56,770 --> 00:57:57,829
- I need to drink. - It's a heartwarming sight.

1554
00:57:57,830 --> 00:57:58,870
I'll close the door.

1555
00:58:01,370 --> 00:58:02,970
You look after your mom.

1556
00:58:03,210 --> 00:58:04,509
I see the resemblance.

1557
00:58:04,510 --> 00:58:05,709
- He looks the same. - He has her nose and mouth.

1558
00:58:05,710 --> 00:58:06,839
- That's right. - Yes.

1559
00:58:06,840 --> 00:58:08,950
Many people tell me that I take after my mom.

1560
00:58:09,210 --> 00:58:12,519
I recently read something.

1561
00:58:12,520 --> 00:58:15,850
Mom finds her children beautiful because they're like...

1562
00:58:16,220 --> 00:58:18,859
a time machine that takes her back to her most beautiful days.

1563
00:58:18,860 --> 00:58:20,390
(They're like a time machine.)

1564
00:58:21,160 --> 00:58:22,529
They have their mom's face.

1565
00:58:22,530 --> 00:58:24,789
It's a way to see herself...

1566
00:58:24,790 --> 00:58:27,199
- in her most beautiful days. - You're right.

1567
00:58:27,200 --> 00:58:29,829
Seeing them together reminds me of those words.

1568
00:58:29,830 --> 00:58:30,830
I see.

1569
00:58:30,831 --> 00:58:32,369
My mom gets angry...

1570
00:58:32,370 --> 00:58:34,469
when people say that I take after her.

1571
00:58:34,470 --> 00:58:35,709
- "Why..." - Your mom gets angry?

1572
00:58:35,710 --> 00:58:37,740
Yes. "Why do you say that he takes after me?"

1573
00:58:38,240 --> 00:58:39,810
- It depends on the mom. - Yes.

1574
00:58:41,410 --> 00:58:42,810
Turn on the heater, Mom.

1575
00:58:44,010 --> 00:58:45,579
Is your body okay? Doesn't it feel heavy?

1576
00:58:45,580 --> 00:58:46,750
My body is okay.

1577
00:58:49,650 --> 00:58:50,650
Let's go.

1578
00:58:50,651 --> 00:58:52,320
(They head home.)

1579
00:58:52,560 --> 00:58:57,289
Tomorrow is the first anniversary of you passing the announcer exam.

1580
00:58:57,290 --> 00:58:58,329
Tomorrow?

1581
00:58:58,330 --> 00:59:01,560
(Seoul is as welcomed as the news of her son passing the exam.)

1582
00:59:01,800 --> 00:59:03,569
I love this song so much.

1583
00:59:03,570 --> 00:59:04,830
I sing it very often.

1584
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:08,240
Kang Yong is attentive.

1585
00:59:10,040 --> 00:59:12,440
(The playlist he put together for his mom is a success.)

1586
00:59:13,080 --> 00:59:15,810
- Mom, you need to get off first. - Okay.

1587
00:59:16,010 --> 00:59:17,280
Get off first.

1588
00:59:18,350 --> 00:59:21,480
(She listens to her son and gets off quickly.)

1589
00:59:22,520 --> 00:59:23,649
Let's go.

1590
00:59:23,650 --> 00:59:26,860
(Let's go.)

1591
00:59:28,830 --> 00:59:30,630
- Let's go. - All right.

1592
00:59:31,060 --> 00:59:32,159
The doors to the netherworld opened.

1593
00:59:32,160 --> 00:59:33,229
She's here for inspection.

1594
00:59:33,230 --> 00:59:34,670
- He'll get a bomb of advice. - Yes.

1595
00:59:37,143 --> 00:59:38,213
Let's go.

1596
00:59:39,213 --> 00:59:41,313
(Nervous)

1597
00:59:41,383 --> 00:59:42,753
It's fragrant, right?

1598
00:59:43,553 --> 00:59:45,222
- Can you smell it? - It smells nice.

1599
00:59:45,223 --> 00:59:46,223
- Yes, it smells nice. - My goodness.

1600
00:59:46,224 --> 00:59:48,122
You put eggs on top of the stove.

1601
00:59:48,123 --> 00:59:49,123
My goodness.

1602
00:59:49,124 --> 00:59:50,422
It began as soon as she arrived.

1603
00:59:50,423 --> 00:59:51,692
She started off lightly.

1604
00:59:51,693 --> 00:59:52,892
It smells nice, right?

1605
00:59:52,893 --> 00:59:53,922
(My goodness)

1606
00:59:53,923 --> 00:59:55,863
- It has been a while, so... - It smells nice.

1607
00:59:56,833 --> 00:59:58,833
- You distract her with fragrance. - Yes.

1608
00:59:59,303 --> 01:00:00,832
- It only smells nice. - "It only smells nice."

1609
01:00:00,833 --> 01:00:02,593
It smells nice since I've cleaned the house.

1610
01:00:02,903 --> 01:00:04,679
It smells nice since you've cleaned the house.

1611
01:00:04,703 --> 01:00:06,903
Mom, give me your coat. I'll hang it up.

1612
01:00:07,373 --> 01:00:09,612
- It's okay. Hold on. - I kept talking to her...

1613
01:00:09,613 --> 01:00:12,313
- in order to distract her. - You tried to distract her.

1614
01:00:13,713 --> 01:00:15,393
It's your first time seeing Wilson, right?

1615
01:00:16,083 --> 01:00:18,012
(He distracts her with Wilson this time.)

1616
01:00:18,013 --> 01:00:19,922
Wilson is here. I can't believe it.

1617
01:00:19,923 --> 01:00:22,053
- Hug it. - I can't believe it.

1618
01:00:22,453 --> 01:00:24,052
I saw it on TV all the time.

1619
01:00:24,053 --> 01:00:26,223
I wanted to hug it.

1620
01:00:26,593 --> 01:00:28,339
- He succeeded in distracting her. - Come here.

1621
01:00:28,363 --> 01:00:30,033
- It was a good strategy. - Yes.

1622
01:00:30,893 --> 01:00:32,833
Nice to meet you, Wilson.

1623
01:00:33,503 --> 01:00:35,333
I thought I'd only see it on TV.

1624
01:00:35,603 --> 01:00:37,903
I got to hug Wilson thanks to my son.

1625
01:00:38,273 --> 01:00:39,793
Mom, this is the jacket you bought me.

1626
01:00:40,873 --> 01:00:41,943
It's pretty.

1627
01:00:42,413 --> 01:00:43,442
It's neat, right?

1628
01:00:43,443 --> 01:00:44,512
- You wore it on purpose. - It's neat.

1629
01:00:44,513 --> 01:00:46,442
- That's right. - You keep talking to her...

1630
01:00:46,443 --> 01:00:48,723
- so that she can't look around. - I keep talking to her.

1631
01:00:49,913 --> 01:00:51,582
You don't give her time to nag at you.

1632
01:00:51,583 --> 01:00:52,883
- Nice. - Let's take a look.

1633
01:00:53,223 --> 01:00:55,493
Mom, take a seat.

1634
01:00:56,923 --> 01:00:58,192
The house is cleaner than you thought, right?

1635
01:00:58,193 --> 01:00:59,563
There's hair on the floor.

1636
01:00:59,763 --> 01:01:01,022
- It can't be like your place. - You got caught.

1637
01:01:01,023 --> 01:01:02,332
Do you have a lint roller?

1638
01:01:02,333 --> 01:01:04,533
I do, but I can vacuum the floor.

1639
01:01:05,603 --> 01:01:07,162
(Cutting)

1640
01:01:07,163 --> 01:01:08,833
Why have you brought so much?

1641
01:01:10,533 --> 01:01:11,772
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1642
01:01:11,773 --> 01:01:12,843
Oh, my gosh.

1643
01:01:13,503 --> 01:01:14,503
What is all this? Let's go over them one by one.

1644
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,042
This is the yakbap.

1645
01:01:16,043 --> 01:01:17,143
- Yakbap? - Yes.

1646
01:01:17,973 --> 01:01:18,982
Here.

1647
01:01:18,983 --> 01:01:20,143
(Excited)

1648
01:01:20,443 --> 01:01:22,353
- They all got squished on the way. - Gosh!

1649
01:01:22,583 --> 01:01:23,653
How did she make that?

1650
01:01:24,153 --> 01:01:26,682
Ever since I was in elementary school,

1651
01:01:26,683 --> 01:01:30,393
my mother made yakbap in the exact same way.

1652
01:01:30,493 --> 01:01:31,692
- It must taste amazing. - It's great.

1653
01:01:31,693 --> 01:01:33,533
It looks like it was made at a rice cake shop.

1654
01:01:34,193 --> 01:01:36,193
- This is glutinous rice, right? - Yes.

1655
01:01:36,633 --> 01:01:37,993
It must taste good to have it now.

1656
01:01:38,263 --> 01:01:39,562
It will taste good now.

1657
01:01:39,563 --> 01:01:41,003
This is homemade kimchi.

1658
01:01:41,363 --> 01:01:42,403
This tastes great.

1659
01:01:42,503 --> 01:01:44,333
Gosh, that looks good.

1660
01:01:45,203 --> 01:01:47,103
(Grabbing)

1661
01:01:47,543 --> 01:01:49,312
(He puts it straight into his mouth.)

1662
01:01:49,313 --> 01:01:50,443
The kimchi tastes so good.

1663
01:01:50,573 --> 01:01:51,682
- Does it taste good? - Yes.

1664
01:01:51,683 --> 01:01:53,443
(Feeling proud)

1665
01:01:53,683 --> 01:01:56,052
No matter what kind of good kimchi I get from elsewhere,

1666
01:01:56,053 --> 01:01:57,953
it tastes different from my mom's kimchi.

1667
01:01:58,113 --> 01:01:59,153
There's a big difference.

1668
01:01:59,323 --> 01:02:00,953
Try some of the meat.

1669
01:02:01,153 --> 01:02:02,693
- Gosh, it's jangjorim! - Jangjorim!

1670
01:02:03,493 --> 01:02:05,662
- Here's some suyuk. - That's great.

1671
01:02:05,663 --> 01:02:06,893
I didn't bring that much.

1672
01:02:07,223 --> 01:02:09,063
- Kimchi? - This is raw skate.

1673
01:02:09,163 --> 01:02:10,993
Gosh, seasoned raw skate!

1674
01:02:11,293 --> 01:02:13,209
- This is the braised skate. - Your signature dish.

1675
01:02:13,233 --> 01:02:14,663
Two pieces of braised skate.

1676
01:02:14,933 --> 01:02:16,073
What's this? Buchimgae?

1677
01:02:16,603 --> 01:02:17,702
- No way. - Shrimp jeon.

1678
01:02:17,703 --> 01:02:19,043
It's like a holiday.

1679
01:02:20,073 --> 01:02:22,473
How many dishes have you brought?

1680
01:02:23,473 --> 01:02:25,142
(She even brought the soft persimmon that she peeled herself.)

1681
01:02:25,143 --> 01:02:26,812
She peeled the soft persimmon?

1682
01:02:26,813 --> 01:02:28,613
She scooped all of it into the bowl.

1683
01:02:29,083 --> 01:02:30,683
(Feeling grateful)

1684
01:02:31,723 --> 01:02:33,223
She's an excellent cook.

1685
01:02:34,753 --> 01:02:36,023
Gosh, are you serious?

1686
01:02:36,293 --> 01:02:38,763
The size of the dishes is perfect for someone living alone.

1687
01:02:39,593 --> 01:02:41,022
She packed them into reasonable portions.

1688
01:02:41,023 --> 01:02:42,433
Right.

1689
01:02:42,593 --> 01:02:43,792
That's perfect for someone living alone.

1690
01:02:43,793 --> 01:02:45,662
It's just enough with a bowl of rice.

1691
01:02:45,663 --> 01:02:47,703
- That's so considerate of her. - Right.

1692
01:02:48,033 --> 01:02:49,233
That's amazing.

1693
01:02:49,433 --> 01:02:50,533
Right.

1694
01:02:51,073 --> 01:02:52,943
But there's something else.

1695
01:02:53,343 --> 01:02:55,173
- The wall feels empty here. - Right.

1696
01:02:56,073 --> 01:02:58,742
- What did you bring? - I brought something to hang up.

1697
01:02:58,743 --> 01:02:59,813
Also,

1698
01:03:00,513 --> 01:03:02,182
- A photo? - place this at the entrance.

1699
01:03:02,183 --> 01:03:03,612
- Gosh! - It's a lucky broom.

1700
01:03:03,613 --> 01:03:04,682
A lucky broom?

1701
01:03:04,683 --> 01:03:06,443
- Here. - I thought it was a bottle of wine.

1702
01:03:06,683 --> 01:03:08,153
No. It's a lucky broom.

1703
01:03:09,023 --> 01:03:10,293
(Touching)

1704
01:03:11,623 --> 01:03:14,692
I think it was since this summer.

1705
01:03:14,693 --> 01:03:15,862
She started learning fabric art.

1706
01:03:15,863 --> 01:03:17,463
So she made that.

1707
01:03:17,693 --> 01:03:18,933
She takes classes twice a week.

1708
01:03:19,103 --> 01:03:20,832
It's literally drawing on fabric.

1709
01:03:20,833 --> 01:03:22,032
She usually draws plants.

1710
01:03:22,033 --> 01:03:24,472
But she has a great talent in drawing.

1711
01:03:24,473 --> 01:03:26,873
She has a great artistic touch.

1712
01:03:27,343 --> 01:03:28,743
Should I put it up here?

1713
01:03:29,143 --> 01:03:30,572
No. I think it'll look better here.

1714
01:03:30,573 --> 01:03:32,042
I think it can be put up here.

1715
01:03:32,043 --> 01:03:33,743
- There? Sure. - Yes.

1716
01:03:33,883 --> 01:03:36,982
The lucky broom represents sweeping in luck.

1717
01:03:36,983 --> 01:03:38,053
Very lightly.

1718
01:03:38,623 --> 01:03:40,063
There you go. That should be enough.

1719
01:03:40,483 --> 01:03:42,093
It has to be stuck right away.

1720
01:03:42,823 --> 01:03:43,923
Will it work?

1721
01:03:44,193 --> 01:03:45,462
- Yes. - Did it work?

1722
01:03:45,463 --> 01:03:46,563
It worked.

1723
01:03:47,193 --> 01:03:48,332
It looks nice.

1724
01:03:48,333 --> 01:03:49,463
It suits the house.

1725
01:03:50,763 --> 01:03:52,333
- No. - The smaller one should go here.

1726
01:03:53,033 --> 01:03:54,873
The bigger one there and the smaller one here.

1727
01:03:56,103 --> 01:03:59,303
(Reaching out)

1728
01:03:59,903 --> 01:04:01,172
(His mother's fabric art frames fill the wall.)

1729
01:04:01,173 --> 01:04:02,473
She brought her work.

1730
01:04:03,073 --> 01:04:04,113
Awesome.

1731
01:04:04,443 --> 01:04:06,212
- She drew them herself. - Really?

1732
01:04:06,213 --> 01:04:07,773
The one on the right looks really nice.

1733
01:04:08,653 --> 01:04:10,352
Instead of going with the same style,

1734
01:04:10,353 --> 01:04:12,913
I think she will do really well with whatever she wants to draw.

1735
01:04:16,053 --> 01:04:17,593
Don't you have some tea for me?

1736
01:04:17,893 --> 01:04:18,963
- Tea? - Yes.

1737
01:04:19,993 --> 01:04:21,162
- Tea? - Yes.

1738
01:04:21,163 --> 01:04:22,292
She suddenly asked for some tea.

1739
01:04:22,293 --> 01:04:23,733
- Tea. - Do you want some tea?

1740
01:04:24,033 --> 01:04:25,663
Yes. Actually...

1741
01:04:26,103 --> 01:04:27,303
Did you bring something?

1742
01:04:27,533 --> 01:04:30,303
I brought the tea mats that I made as well.

1743
01:04:30,633 --> 01:04:32,672
It would be nice to have some tea with these.

1744
01:04:32,673 --> 01:04:34,002
She wanted to use those.

1745
01:04:34,003 --> 01:04:35,403
- She wanted to use those? - Right.

1746
01:04:37,143 --> 01:04:38,813
While having some coffee...

1747
01:04:38,913 --> 01:04:40,583
- Would you like some coffee? - Yes.

1748
01:04:43,353 --> 01:04:44,553
Do you not have any wet wipes?

1749
01:04:44,753 --> 01:04:46,253
- I do, Mom. - Where?

1750
01:04:46,653 --> 01:04:47,782
Right here.

1751
01:04:47,783 --> 01:04:49,852
(Pass me the wet wipes.)

1752
01:04:49,853 --> 01:04:50,893
Gosh.

1753
01:04:51,893 --> 01:04:53,093
She's going to start cleaning.

1754
01:04:53,763 --> 01:04:54,823
Gosh.

1755
01:04:56,093 --> 01:04:58,293
- It has begun. - She's cleaning that part?

1756
01:04:59,633 --> 01:05:01,733
It must've been here for a while. It won't come off.

1757
01:05:02,133 --> 01:05:03,202
It's the part under the table...

1758
01:05:03,203 --> 01:05:04,363
- when you carry it. - Right.

1759
01:05:04,773 --> 01:05:06,803
Right at that moment when he left the room.

1760
01:05:07,303 --> 01:05:08,873
(Walking on eggshells)

1761
01:05:08,973 --> 01:05:11,983
That's just a trace of me, Mom.

1762
01:05:12,643 --> 01:05:14,882
These unclean traces don't need to be left.

1763
01:05:14,883 --> 01:05:16,153
Gosh, it has begun.

1764
01:05:16,283 --> 01:05:17,412
The battle has begun.

1765
01:05:17,413 --> 01:05:18,753
(He starts feeling anxious.)

1766
01:05:19,123 --> 01:05:20,753
(Sighing)

1767
01:05:21,823 --> 01:05:23,052
I should've brought the drinks quickly.

1768
01:05:23,053 --> 01:05:24,253
Right.

1769
01:05:27,293 --> 01:05:29,463
This is what's fascinating about all mothers.

1770
01:05:29,633 --> 01:05:32,533
- They use wet wipes really well. - Right.

1771
01:05:32,763 --> 01:05:34,162
They use one sheet...

1772
01:05:34,163 --> 01:05:35,603
- for several hours. - Right.

1773
01:05:37,533 --> 01:05:38,902
It's a bit...

1774
01:05:38,903 --> 01:05:40,503
(She places the coasters nicely.)

1775
01:05:40,603 --> 01:05:41,743
Why did you place three?

1776
01:05:42,873 --> 01:05:44,543
- Is this for Wilson? - Yes.

1777
01:05:45,213 --> 01:05:46,413
The house is neat, isn't it?

1778
01:05:47,713 --> 01:05:49,152
It's neater than you thought,

1779
01:05:49,153 --> 01:05:50,153
- right? - Sure.

1780
01:05:50,154 --> 01:05:51,383
(Chuckling)

1781
01:05:52,523 --> 01:05:55,293
(I'll sit next to Mom.)

1782
01:05:55,653 --> 01:05:57,893
(She takes a sip of the warm tea her son made.)

1783
01:05:58,823 --> 01:06:01,063
(I'll take a sip as well.)

1784
01:06:01,393 --> 01:06:02,593
Let's clean up.

1785
01:06:03,233 --> 01:06:05,203
These should go in the trash.

1786
01:06:07,233 --> 01:06:08,773
I clean up right away, Mom.

1787
01:06:09,433 --> 01:06:10,472
The sink.

1788
01:06:10,473 --> 01:06:12,843
- I clean up right away. - I need to take a look.

1789
01:06:12,973 --> 01:06:14,302
"Give me some credit, Mom."

1790
01:06:14,303 --> 01:06:15,823
Look. I clean up like this right away.

1791
01:06:16,143 --> 01:06:17,313
"I've changed."

1792
01:06:17,643 --> 01:06:19,512
(Sighing)

1793
01:06:19,513 --> 01:06:21,643
(Looking around)

1794
01:06:22,013 --> 01:06:23,082
(His heart sinks at the sound of his mother's sigh.)

1795
01:06:23,083 --> 01:06:25,553
- "Look at this." - She shouldn't see the gas stove.

1796
01:06:26,553 --> 01:06:27,653
Hold on.

1797
01:06:28,493 --> 01:06:30,392
Honestly, can't I be allowed to clean this once?

1798
01:06:30,393 --> 01:06:31,622
- Gosh, she spotted it. - There.

1799
01:06:31,623 --> 01:06:33,769
- It doesn't need to be cleaned. - Bring me the rag I brought.

1800
01:06:33,793 --> 01:06:34,923
It won't come off.

1801
01:06:36,133 --> 01:06:37,193
Moms can make it come off.

1802
01:06:39,233 --> 01:06:40,762
(She makes a check for the closet under the sink.)

1803
01:06:40,763 --> 01:06:44,102
I tidied up this area last time.

1804
01:06:44,103 --> 01:06:45,342
- It's a mess again. - She's performing an inspection.

1805
01:06:45,343 --> 01:06:46,573
It has begun.

1806
01:06:47,673 --> 01:06:49,143
Gosh.

1807
01:06:50,513 --> 01:06:53,283
(Walking on eggshells)

1808
01:06:54,743 --> 01:06:55,782
Gosh.

1809
01:06:55,783 --> 01:06:57,753
I tell her not to do it,

1810
01:06:58,583 --> 01:07:00,723
but she cleans everything whenever she comes.

1811
01:07:00,983 --> 01:07:02,653
- My goodness. - She couldn't be stopped.

1812
01:07:03,323 --> 01:07:04,653
She can't stand it.

1813
01:07:05,593 --> 01:07:06,692
Hold on.

1814
01:07:06,693 --> 01:07:08,613
(He heads somewhere while walking on eggshells.)

1815
01:07:09,533 --> 01:07:12,663
(Kang Yong gets something out from the microwave.)

1816
01:07:13,763 --> 01:07:15,033
Mom, try the walnut cake.

1817
01:07:15,833 --> 01:07:17,309
- He's trying to distract her. - It's really good.

1818
01:07:17,333 --> 01:07:18,403
He's blocking her mouth.

1819
01:07:18,573 --> 01:07:20,073
(She lets him put it in her mouth.)

1820
01:07:20,873 --> 01:07:22,813
It's hot, right? It's good.

1821
01:07:23,013 --> 01:07:25,089
- Isn't it too hot for her? - Does it have red beans in it?

1822
01:07:25,113 --> 01:07:26,382
It's hot.

1823
01:07:26,383 --> 01:07:28,553
(It's hot.)

1824
01:07:28,653 --> 01:07:30,113
Look over here.

1825
01:07:30,283 --> 01:07:31,513
(Giving up)

1826
01:07:31,653 --> 01:07:34,682
- Gosh, it's hot. - He's really walking on eggshells.

1827
01:07:34,683 --> 01:07:36,452
Don't you become like that? I'm the same.

1828
01:07:36,453 --> 01:07:37,622
- Well, I just... - When my mom starts cleaning,

1829
01:07:37,623 --> 01:07:38,822
I feel anxious.

1830
01:07:38,823 --> 01:07:39,993
- Really? - Yes.

1831
01:07:40,963 --> 01:07:42,033
Hold on.

1832
01:07:42,533 --> 01:07:44,562
- Lift the coffee machine. - This?

1833
01:07:44,563 --> 01:07:45,633
Yes.

1834
01:07:45,963 --> 01:07:47,162
She might end up cleaning the whole house...

1835
01:07:47,163 --> 01:07:48,363
starting with that.

1836
01:07:48,703 --> 01:07:51,232
My goodness! This part is the worst!

1837
01:07:51,233 --> 01:07:52,302
Be careful.

1838
01:07:52,303 --> 01:07:54,143
Gosh, unbelievable.

1839
01:07:54,243 --> 01:07:55,412
This part...

1840
01:07:55,413 --> 01:07:56,943
- Gosh. - Forget it. I'll do it.

1841
01:07:57,073 --> 01:07:58,643
I washed this in the morning.

1842
01:07:59,543 --> 01:08:00,682
I'll wash them later.

1843
01:08:00,683 --> 01:08:02,112
(His mom starts washing the dishes.)

1844
01:08:02,113 --> 01:08:03,152
I'll do it.

1845
01:08:03,153 --> 01:08:04,673
- She hasn't even begun. - I'll do it.

1846
01:08:05,013 --> 01:08:06,893
I'll do it. It needs to be done with dish soap.

1847
01:08:07,523 --> 01:08:10,093
(The son's calls are useless to the mother.)

1848
01:08:10,423 --> 01:08:11,492
This will be put away.

1849
01:08:11,493 --> 01:08:12,662
(The dishes are washed in a flash.)

1850
01:08:12,663 --> 01:08:14,993
Done. Done, right?

1851
01:08:16,333 --> 01:08:17,709
- I need to check the bathroom. - The bathroom is fine.

1852
01:08:17,733 --> 01:08:19,479
- I need to check the bathroom. - The bathroom is fine.

1853
01:08:19,503 --> 01:08:20,532
The bathroom.

1854
01:08:20,533 --> 01:08:22,003
(Feeling anxious)

1855
01:08:22,203 --> 01:08:23,372
Gosh.

1856
01:08:23,373 --> 01:08:25,032
(I have to clean it all over.)

1857
01:08:25,033 --> 01:08:26,742
I felt bad about it.

1858
01:08:26,743 --> 01:08:28,572
- Of course. - I tried to stop her,

1859
01:08:28,573 --> 01:08:30,289
- but she wouldn't listen. - As it might be too exhausting?

1860
01:08:30,313 --> 01:08:31,342
Right.

1861
01:08:31,343 --> 01:08:33,843
Look at the toilet getting cleaned.

1862
01:08:34,643 --> 01:08:37,352
I tell her not to do it, but she won't listen.

1863
01:08:37,353 --> 01:08:38,683
Gosh.

1864
01:08:39,083 --> 01:08:40,699
She cleans things until she gets satisfied.

1865
01:08:40,723 --> 01:08:41,823
In the end,

1866
01:08:42,153 --> 01:08:43,322
I thought it was better to give her a massage...

1867
01:08:43,323 --> 01:08:44,423
while she worked.

1868
01:08:44,993 --> 01:08:46,093
My mom can't be stopped.

1869
01:08:46,363 --> 01:08:47,423
That's enough, Mom.

1870
01:08:47,723 --> 01:08:50,162
This is a method I figured out.

1871
01:08:50,163 --> 01:08:52,162
"Mom, don't do it!"

1872
01:08:52,163 --> 01:08:53,703
- This will never work. - Right.

1873
01:08:54,163 --> 01:08:56,503
That is why I prepare a gift for her instead.

1874
01:08:56,833 --> 01:08:58,572
- My mom draws as well. - Right.

1875
01:08:58,573 --> 01:09:00,972
When I suggest going to an art supply store...

1876
01:09:00,973 --> 01:09:02,312
that is nearby,

1877
01:09:02,313 --> 01:09:03,573
she stops cleaning right away.

1878
01:09:03,773 --> 01:09:05,982
- You go for her greatest interest? - She stops right at that moment.

1879
01:09:05,983 --> 01:09:07,559
So you bring up your mother's greatest interest.

1880
01:09:07,583 --> 01:09:09,852
How does a treasure hunt sound?

1881
01:09:09,853 --> 01:09:11,452
Bills can be hidden around the house for her.

1882
01:09:11,453 --> 01:09:12,522
That's a great idea!

1883
01:09:12,523 --> 01:09:13,752
- That's the worst! - Whenever she cleans something,

1884
01:09:13,753 --> 01:09:15,229
- she'll find a bill. - Is his mother a mole?

1885
01:09:15,253 --> 01:09:16,892
- No. - Is his mother a mole?

1886
01:09:16,893 --> 01:09:18,739
That can be done if there's no way to stop her.

1887
01:09:18,763 --> 01:09:19,862
Is his mother a mole or what?

1888
01:09:19,863 --> 01:09:21,439
(That can be a fun way to be a good son.)

1889
01:09:21,463 --> 01:09:22,562
That's enough.

1890
01:09:22,563 --> 01:09:25,133
I'll clean that later.

1891
01:09:25,503 --> 01:09:27,583
- Will you really clean it? - Yes. I'll do it later.

1892
01:09:27,733 --> 01:09:29,803
- I'm going to come and check. - Okay.

1893
01:09:31,403 --> 01:09:32,472
Look at how clean it is now.

1894
01:09:32,473 --> 01:09:33,873
You should've taken off your socks.

1895
01:09:34,103 --> 01:09:36,043
It's okay.

1896
01:09:36,473 --> 01:09:37,712
That part is fine.

1897
01:09:37,713 --> 01:09:39,242
(Mom's cleaning won't end.)

1898
01:09:39,243 --> 01:09:41,512
What are you talking about? This part is the worst.

1899
01:09:41,513 --> 01:09:43,029
(What are you talking about? This part is the worst.)

1900
01:09:43,053 --> 01:09:44,553
That's enough, Mom.

1901
01:09:44,913 --> 01:09:47,582
Pass me the lint roller later.

1902
01:09:47,583 --> 01:09:48,953
- Okay. - The white one.

1903
01:09:49,853 --> 01:09:51,053
- Let's see. - That's enough.

1904
01:09:51,693 --> 01:09:52,893
It's clean now, right?

1905
01:09:53,293 --> 01:09:55,792
This should all be brought down to be cleaned,

1906
01:09:55,793 --> 01:09:58,563
but I don't want to be going through your things.

1907
01:09:58,663 --> 01:10:00,303
Would you like an MBC diary, Mom?

1908
01:10:00,803 --> 01:10:01,933
Give me one.

1909
01:10:02,773 --> 01:10:04,072
- I got it recently. - I kept talking to her.

1910
01:10:04,073 --> 01:10:07,073
- Kang Yong knows what to do. - I constantly got her interest.

1911
01:10:07,173 --> 01:10:08,643
Mothers love diaries.

1912
01:10:09,243 --> 01:10:10,342
Check this out.

1913
01:10:10,343 --> 01:10:11,689
(There's something else I want to show you, Mom.)

1914
01:10:11,713 --> 01:10:12,843
"Election 2025."

1915
01:10:12,943 --> 01:10:14,443
- These were your lines? - Yes.

1916
01:10:15,653 --> 01:10:17,913
You'll be Kang Da Eun. I'll be me.

1917
01:10:18,553 --> 01:10:20,053
Look. I'll start.

1918
01:10:20,753 --> 01:10:25,123
(The actual script her son used with his partner)

1919
01:10:25,623 --> 01:10:27,362
The election race is heading toward the finish line.

1920
01:10:27,363 --> 01:10:29,132
I'm here as the final commentator.

1921
01:10:29,133 --> 01:10:30,362
I'm Ko Kang Yong.

1922
01:10:30,363 --> 01:10:31,483
(His mother starts smiling.)

1923
01:10:31,893 --> 01:10:33,502
I'm Kang Da Eun.

1924
01:10:33,503 --> 01:10:35,203
It isn't over yet, everyone.

1925
01:10:35,403 --> 01:10:38,002
- She has a great voice. - The real race starts now.

1926
01:10:38,003 --> 01:10:39,603
No. You have to sound more enthusiastic.

1927
01:10:40,003 --> 01:10:41,602
The election race is heading toward the finish line.

1928
01:10:41,603 --> 01:10:42,912
I'm here as the final commentator.

1929
01:10:42,913 --> 01:10:43,942
I'm Ko Kang Yong.

1930
01:10:43,943 --> 01:10:45,242
- I'm Kang Da Eun. - Right.

1931
01:10:45,243 --> 01:10:47,113
- It isn't over yet, everyone. - There you go.

1932
01:10:47,283 --> 01:10:49,883
- The real race starts now. - Right.

1933
01:10:50,613 --> 01:10:52,522
- She's great at that. - Her voice sounds very young.

1934
01:10:52,523 --> 01:10:53,652
- Right. - I'm serious.

1935
01:10:53,653 --> 01:10:55,052
- Her voice hasn't changed at all. - Right.

1936
01:10:55,053 --> 01:10:56,722
It was my dream to become a voice actress.

1937
01:10:56,723 --> 01:10:57,892
I wanted to become one.

1938
01:10:57,893 --> 01:10:59,663
- She has a great voice. - I love her tone.

1939
01:11:00,693 --> 01:11:02,992
(She starts chuckling after forgetting about the cleaning.)

1940
01:11:02,993 --> 01:11:04,532
- Gosh. - Cleaning is over now.

1941
01:11:04,533 --> 01:11:05,703
We have to head out to eat.

1942
01:11:06,133 --> 01:11:07,863
I made a reservation.

1943
01:11:08,103 --> 01:11:09,233
Did he make a reservation?

1944
01:11:10,433 --> 01:11:12,003
(Approaching)

1945
01:11:12,943 --> 01:11:14,503
(Helping her)

1946
01:11:15,243 --> 01:11:18,143
(She gets ready to leave with her son's help.)

1947
01:11:19,043 --> 01:11:20,143
I'm feeling great.

1948
01:11:20,443 --> 01:11:21,813
- I'll get my bag. - Right.

1949
01:11:23,383 --> 01:11:24,912
Let's tidy this up.

1950
01:11:24,913 --> 01:11:27,283
I'll sort them out. I'll put the T-shirts away.

1951
01:11:28,183 --> 01:11:31,223
- I'll put them away. - I want to clear out everything.

1952
01:11:31,393 --> 01:11:33,763
I'll do it when you go home. We have to eat.

1953
01:11:34,123 --> 01:11:35,662
Take a picture with Wilson.

1954
01:11:35,663 --> 01:11:36,893
Oh, right.

1955
01:11:37,663 --> 01:11:38,832
- Like this? - Yes.

1956
01:11:38,833 --> 01:11:40,333
(Laughing)

1957
01:11:40,463 --> 01:11:41,463
Done.

1958
01:11:41,863 --> 01:11:44,533
- He changed the subject again. - Kang Yong knows what to do.

1959
01:11:44,573 --> 01:11:46,343
He's really good at it.

1960
01:11:49,343 --> 01:11:53,243
(They head out to eat after cleaning the house.)

1961
01:11:55,113 --> 01:11:59,183
Gosh! They're setting up a tree! It looks amazing.

1962
01:12:01,483 --> 01:12:03,452
- Right. - Hyun Moo did his running here.

1963
01:12:03,453 --> 01:12:05,192
- Around here. - Was it here?

1964
01:12:05,193 --> 01:12:07,593
Oh, right! He went past Gwanghwamun.

1965
01:12:08,093 --> 01:12:09,133
What?

1966
01:12:10,363 --> 01:12:11,863
Gosh, I laughed so much.

1967
01:12:12,363 --> 01:12:13,502
(They head somewhere past Gwanghwamun.)

1968
01:12:13,503 --> 01:12:14,932
He said, "I Live Alone is great."

1969
01:12:14,933 --> 01:12:16,033
- Dad said that? - Right.

1970
01:12:19,343 --> 01:12:21,603
(They sing together her favorite song.)

1971
01:12:22,713 --> 01:12:25,612
(Will we be able to love?)

1972
01:12:25,613 --> 01:12:26,742
(Singing)

1973
01:12:26,743 --> 01:12:29,112
I can't sing out loud right now.

1974
01:12:29,113 --> 01:12:31,053
- You just did, Mom. - I did?

1975
01:12:33,253 --> 01:12:36,492
I'm someone who can sing "Tears" by So Chan Whee.

1976
01:12:36,493 --> 01:12:37,752
Gosh, really?

1977
01:12:37,753 --> 01:12:39,033
Is she the master of high notes?

1978
01:12:39,093 --> 01:12:42,932
(That is just the love that is felt)

1979
01:12:42,933 --> 01:12:44,232
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1980
01:12:44,233 --> 01:12:45,713
She sings the high notes really well.

1981
01:12:46,063 --> 01:12:47,343
- You can hit them now. - Right.

1982
01:12:49,573 --> 01:12:52,243
(They arrive at Hongdae after her passionate singing.)

1983
01:12:52,543 --> 01:12:54,343
- Should I get off? - Yes. Get off carefully.

1984
01:12:54,443 --> 01:12:56,473
- To the left, Mom. - Right.

1985
01:12:57,613 --> 01:13:00,342
(They head into a building.)

1986
01:13:00,343 --> 01:13:02,353
- Here it is. - Is it a restaurant? Am I wrong?

1987
01:13:03,770 --> 01:13:05,609
- Hello. - Hello.

1988
01:13:05,610 --> 01:13:07,239
Can we get your name which you made a reservation with?

1989
01:13:07,240 --> 01:13:09,439
Right. I made a reservation under Ko Kang Yong.

1990
01:13:09,440 --> 01:13:11,056
- I will lead you to your table. - Right.

1991
01:13:11,080 --> 01:13:12,579
Is it a steak restaurant?

1992
01:13:12,580 --> 01:13:14,510
I chose this place with care.

1993
01:13:19,150 --> 01:13:21,520
(The place Kang Yong made a reservation for)

1994
01:13:21,860 --> 01:13:23,759
I chose a fine dining restaurant.

1995
01:13:23,760 --> 01:13:27,159
I prepared a course meal for my mother.

1996
01:13:27,160 --> 01:13:28,259
Great job.

1997
01:13:28,260 --> 01:13:31,060
My mom and dad always go to the same places.

1998
01:13:31,470 --> 01:13:33,129
It's always the same sundae gukbap place...

1999
01:13:33,130 --> 01:13:34,869
and the same bean sprout gukbap place.

2000
01:13:34,870 --> 01:13:37,000
So we went to Jeonju together,

2001
01:13:37,570 --> 01:13:39,539
and I treated them to a fine dining meal...

2002
01:13:39,540 --> 01:13:42,280
with my MBC bonus.

2003
01:13:42,480 --> 01:13:44,540
- Great job. - It's our second fine dining meal.

2004
01:13:45,450 --> 01:13:47,650
It's the second fine dining meal for both of us.

2005
01:13:49,250 --> 01:13:51,519
It would be great if you could prepare the course meal...

2006
01:13:51,520 --> 01:13:53,190
I made a reservation for.

2007
01:13:54,450 --> 01:13:56,390
I heard the plating here was done beautifully.

2008
01:13:56,760 --> 01:13:59,760
The food is served nicely.

2009
01:14:00,490 --> 01:14:02,759
- It's here. - Right.

2010
01:14:02,760 --> 01:14:03,836
(He chose this restaurant based on his mother's tastes.)

2011
01:14:03,860 --> 01:14:05,429
- Thank you. - Here you are.

2012
01:14:05,430 --> 01:14:07,169
Starting from the amuse-bouche,

2013
01:14:07,170 --> 01:14:09,099
- we will serve you today's dishes. - Right.

2014
01:14:09,100 --> 01:14:11,810
Here are four different finger foods with the cleanser soup.

2015
01:14:12,270 --> 01:14:15,040
- Food must look nice, right? - Yes.

2016
01:14:15,410 --> 01:14:17,079
It would be great to visit those places with your parents...

2017
01:14:17,080 --> 01:14:18,186
- from time to time. - Right.

2018
01:14:18,210 --> 01:14:20,049
Those places shouldn't always be visited with your girlfriend.

2019
01:14:20,050 --> 01:14:21,930
You have to bring your parents to those places.

2020
01:14:22,520 --> 01:14:23,800
Are you saying that to yourself?

2021
01:14:24,180 --> 01:14:25,449
(Flustered)

2022
01:14:25,450 --> 01:14:26,689
- Well... - Why are you talking to yourself?

2023
01:14:26,690 --> 01:14:28,519
Can't you bring me to a place like that?

2024
01:14:28,520 --> 01:14:30,020
Just have some sundaeguk with me.

2025
01:14:31,630 --> 01:14:32,959
How do we eat this?

2026
01:14:32,960 --> 01:14:34,790
Do we use this? Oh, our hands?

2027
01:14:35,230 --> 01:14:36,460
Oh, our hands?

2028
01:14:38,570 --> 01:14:40,670
- Like this? - In one bite.

2029
01:14:40,930 --> 01:14:42,570
(Eating it in one bite)

2030
01:14:43,640 --> 01:14:46,270
Gosh, it's delicious.

2031
01:14:47,540 --> 01:14:49,510
It's good, isn't it?

2032
01:14:50,710 --> 01:14:52,050
That's lovely to see.

2033
01:14:53,180 --> 01:14:56,150
(He takes a bite after seeing his mother enjoy it.)

2034
01:14:56,850 --> 01:14:59,650
I felt nervous about whether she would say it's good.

2035
01:14:59,750 --> 01:15:01,190
- You're a great son. - Gosh.

2036
01:15:01,690 --> 01:15:03,019
I think she was satisfied at this moment.

2037
01:15:03,020 --> 01:15:04,620
Right? It's fascinating.

2038
01:15:05,590 --> 01:15:06,729
It's very refreshing.

2039
01:15:06,730 --> 01:15:07,760
(Relieved)

2040
01:15:08,130 --> 01:15:09,160
It's here.

2041
01:15:10,130 --> 01:15:11,160
Excuse me.

2042
01:15:12,800 --> 01:15:13,800
(Looking carefully)

2043
01:15:13,801 --> 01:15:15,769
The second course is the salad with vegetables...

2044
01:15:15,770 --> 01:15:18,740
and the pita bread with the chimichurri salsa.

2045
01:15:21,370 --> 01:15:23,840
I'm curious about how it tastes as it looks nice.

2046
01:15:27,710 --> 01:15:29,050
(Crunchy)

2047
01:15:29,650 --> 01:15:31,620
It's nice and sour with the beet.

2048
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:35,260
(Grabbing the bread)

2049
01:15:36,160 --> 01:15:37,860
Bring up your spoon. I'll get you some.

2050
01:15:38,690 --> 01:15:40,190
Just a little. That's enough.

2051
01:15:40,790 --> 01:15:42,060
You should have two.

2052
01:15:42,830 --> 01:15:45,130
- You should have two. - It's yours.

2053
01:15:45,300 --> 01:15:46,470
This is beautiful.

2054
01:15:46,800 --> 01:15:48,270
He takes care of his mother well.

2055
01:15:50,670 --> 01:15:51,710
How is it?

2056
01:15:52,840 --> 01:15:54,240
Spring hasn't come yet.

2057
01:15:54,910 --> 01:15:56,739
- It's a feast of spring flowers. - A feast of spring flowers?

2058
01:15:56,740 --> 01:15:58,260
- It's lovely. - What a way to put it.

2059
01:15:58,950 --> 01:16:00,510
My son did well to choose this place.

2060
01:16:00,980 --> 01:16:03,156
- The food must suit her taste. - She's enjoying the food.

2061
01:16:03,180 --> 01:16:04,980
Wasn't there something unique about the food?

2062
01:16:05,050 --> 01:16:06,150
It's delicious.

2063
01:16:06,650 --> 01:16:08,559
There wasn't any seafood or meat.

2064
01:16:08,560 --> 01:16:09,590
- Right. - Right.

2065
01:16:10,020 --> 01:16:11,360
This is a vegan course meal.

2066
01:16:11,760 --> 01:16:13,529
- I see. - It's just made with vegetables.

2067
01:16:13,530 --> 01:16:14,629
- That explains. - It's a vegan meal?

2068
01:16:14,630 --> 01:16:16,059
You always have the steamed cabbage...

2069
01:16:16,060 --> 01:16:17,900
- and vegetables. - Right.

2070
01:16:18,430 --> 01:16:19,969
That makes sense.

2071
01:16:19,970 --> 01:16:21,330
(His mother is vegan.)

2072
01:16:21,870 --> 01:16:24,870
At around October...

2073
01:16:25,710 --> 01:16:27,470
in 2022,

2074
01:16:27,910 --> 01:16:30,510
she was just about to reach the late stage of colorectal cancer.

2075
01:16:31,280 --> 01:16:33,440
She went through anticancer therapy for 3 to 4 months.

2076
01:16:33,680 --> 01:16:37,220
Even after that, she had to rest...

2077
01:16:37,520 --> 01:16:38,690
for a year or two.

2078
01:16:39,190 --> 01:16:40,320
Before all that happened,

2079
01:16:41,150 --> 01:16:43,390
I called her once every three months.

2080
01:16:44,060 --> 01:16:45,860
I visited her once every six months.

2081
01:16:46,590 --> 01:16:47,830
I was a terrible son.

2082
01:16:47,890 --> 01:16:50,410
But after she went through that, I called her every single day.

2083
01:16:51,200 --> 01:16:53,869
I went back home once a week.

2084
01:16:53,870 --> 01:16:55,169
From Busan to Gunsan.

2085
01:16:55,170 --> 01:16:57,570
I suddenly felt that I should be seeing her often.

2086
01:16:58,640 --> 01:17:02,010
That was when I really tried my best to do that.

2087
01:17:03,780 --> 01:17:05,549
After getting diagnosed with colorectal cancer,

2088
01:17:05,550 --> 01:17:07,079
- did her diet change? - Yes.

2089
01:17:07,080 --> 01:17:09,120
She used to love eating meat.

2090
01:17:09,920 --> 01:17:12,319
Every morning,

2091
01:17:12,320 --> 01:17:15,389
she eats cabbage or vegetables.

2092
01:17:15,390 --> 01:17:19,160
That was why I wanted to treat her to a different vegan meal.

2093
01:17:19,960 --> 01:17:22,599
There was a moment when I felt something similar.

2094
01:17:22,600 --> 01:17:23,760
My younger brother said this.

2095
01:17:24,060 --> 01:17:26,769
"You should visit..."

2096
01:17:26,770 --> 01:17:28,740
"at least once a month."

2097
01:17:28,940 --> 01:17:30,100
I asked why and he said this.

2098
01:17:31,440 --> 01:17:34,440
"Even if you visit Mom and Dad once a month,"

2099
01:17:34,570 --> 01:17:35,839
"that's around ten times a year."

2100
01:17:35,840 --> 01:17:38,280
"That's about it."

2101
01:17:38,750 --> 01:17:40,150
That really spoke to me.

2102
01:17:40,780 --> 01:17:43,020
- The numbers made it so clear. - Right.

2103
01:17:43,750 --> 01:17:45,119
- Right. - Right.

2104
01:17:45,120 --> 01:17:47,150
That made me want to visit my parents more often.

2105
01:17:48,150 --> 01:17:49,520
You love eggplants, right?

2106
01:17:49,690 --> 01:17:52,360
I love eggplants. I eat them very often.

2107
01:17:53,360 --> 01:17:54,860
I eat them often.

2108
01:17:56,730 --> 01:17:58,299
Her son got a job...

2109
01:17:58,300 --> 01:17:59,970
and is taking her to these places now.

2110
01:18:00,570 --> 01:18:02,400
(Feeling proud)

2111
01:18:03,000 --> 01:18:05,370
How was last week's news?

2112
01:18:06,070 --> 01:18:08,216
You always look great. It's my son, you're talking about.

2113
01:18:08,240 --> 01:18:10,510
She watches all of my shows.

2114
01:18:10,840 --> 01:18:12,780
I watched your news shows. Also,

2115
01:18:13,610 --> 01:18:15,250
you were in the I Live Alone Field Day.

2116
01:18:15,720 --> 01:18:17,780
I watched that more than 20 times.

2117
01:18:18,280 --> 01:18:20,590
- Gosh. - I barely came out in that.

2118
01:18:20,820 --> 01:18:23,890
This is what I talked about with your dad.

2119
01:18:24,360 --> 01:18:27,160
We wondered how much you would shine...

2120
01:18:28,190 --> 01:18:30,230
while being between famous people.

2121
01:18:30,600 --> 01:18:32,570
When you ran while wearing a suit,

2122
01:18:33,130 --> 01:18:34,269
you started to shine.

2123
01:18:34,270 --> 01:18:36,770
All of my friends called me...

2124
01:18:37,400 --> 01:18:39,509
and worried about you with your messy hair...

2125
01:18:39,510 --> 01:18:41,370
after running in a suit.

2126
01:18:41,610 --> 01:18:45,409
That was why I said, "Didn't that make him shine more?"

2127
01:18:45,410 --> 01:18:46,450
And they all agreed.

2128
01:18:46,780 --> 01:18:48,150
- Right. - Right.

2129
01:18:48,180 --> 01:18:50,119
You were the star of that day, Kang Yong.

2130
01:18:50,120 --> 01:18:52,020
- On that day? - The star of the Field Day.

2131
01:18:52,620 --> 01:18:54,450
This was the moment that made me clap.

2132
01:18:54,720 --> 01:18:56,019
You were an excellent runner.

2133
01:18:56,020 --> 01:18:57,496
- You were so fast. - When I went past Woo Il.

2134
01:18:57,520 --> 01:18:59,030
Gosh, Kang Yong is really fast.

2135
01:18:59,130 --> 01:19:02,330
It's unbelievable that he beat me while wearing a suit.

2136
01:19:03,400 --> 01:19:05,369
So you love seeing your son do well.

2137
01:19:05,370 --> 01:19:07,630
Right. It's the same for all parents.

2138
01:19:08,300 --> 01:19:09,970
All I can see is my son.

2139
01:19:10,300 --> 01:19:12,040
I saw who did what to you.

2140
01:19:13,610 --> 01:19:18,180
Kian84 dusted the flour on you from behind.

2141
01:19:19,550 --> 01:19:20,849
I didn't know that.

2142
01:19:20,850 --> 01:19:22,326
That proves that she watched it over and over.

2143
01:19:22,350 --> 01:19:25,549
Jae Hyeon dusted the flour off of you from front to back.

2144
01:19:25,550 --> 01:19:26,989
- There's a lot on me? - Yes.

2145
01:19:26,990 --> 01:19:28,959
Those are brief moments.

2146
01:19:28,960 --> 01:19:32,190
(Kang Yong is the star in her eyes in every scene.)

2147
01:19:32,730 --> 01:19:35,460
I can see those things naturally.

2148
01:19:36,200 --> 01:19:37,880
Gosh, I should've taken care of Kang Yong.

2149
01:19:39,200 --> 01:19:42,200
I dusted the flour off of you without a word.

2150
01:19:43,500 --> 01:19:45,140
That's something really impressive to do.

2151
01:19:46,670 --> 01:19:47,840
(Smirking)

2152
01:19:48,170 --> 01:19:50,840
Did Hyun Moo not do anything for me?

2153
01:19:51,180 --> 01:19:52,950
When you were running,

2154
01:19:53,250 --> 01:19:54,749
he told everyone to look at you.

2155
01:19:54,750 --> 01:19:56,980
- He said you were running outward. - That was Dae Ho.

2156
01:19:57,150 --> 01:20:00,120
- No. It was Hyun Moo. - Gosh.

2157
01:20:01,350 --> 01:20:03,120
He went past him while running outward!

2158
01:20:04,260 --> 01:20:07,090
- So it really was me who said that. - How does she remember all that?

2159
01:20:08,160 --> 01:20:10,000
I watched it so many times.

2160
01:20:11,400 --> 01:20:13,299
So the ones who took care of me stood out to you.

2161
01:20:13,300 --> 01:20:14,330
Right.

2162
01:20:14,830 --> 01:20:16,840
- I realized that... - That's touching to hear.

2163
01:20:17,370 --> 01:20:19,170
There were a lot of great people around you.

2164
01:20:20,210 --> 01:20:22,880
(The vegan main dish appears.)

2165
01:20:25,650 --> 01:20:26,780
Is this soy meat?

2166
01:20:27,050 --> 01:20:28,950
Yes. It's soy meat.

2167
01:20:29,420 --> 01:20:31,119
It looks like real meat.

2168
01:20:31,120 --> 01:20:32,150
Soy meat?

2169
01:20:33,350 --> 01:20:35,030
It's been a while since I've had soy meat.

2170
01:20:36,120 --> 01:20:39,059
(She softly cuts a piece...)

2171
01:20:39,060 --> 01:20:40,429
(and takes a bite.)

2172
01:20:40,430 --> 01:20:41,490
How is it?

2173
01:20:42,360 --> 01:20:43,430
This is great.

2174
01:20:43,700 --> 01:20:45,199
I'm curious. I've never tried any.

2175
01:20:45,200 --> 01:20:46,720
It tasted just like a short rib patty.

2176
01:20:47,100 --> 01:20:48,570
(Checking her)

2177
01:20:48,700 --> 01:20:50,969
It makes you full even though small portions are served.

2178
01:20:50,970 --> 01:20:52,010
Right.

2179
01:20:52,110 --> 01:20:53,309
I'm slowly starting to get full.

2180
01:20:53,310 --> 01:20:55,380
Of course. This will surely make you full.

2181
01:20:55,610 --> 01:20:57,280
I love meals that are like this.

2182
01:20:57,840 --> 01:21:00,000
- He must've prepared something. - He's getting ready.

2183
01:21:00,050 --> 01:21:01,780
So I kept checking her like that.

2184
01:21:02,150 --> 01:21:03,350
It looks so obvious.

2185
01:21:04,850 --> 01:21:07,190
- I will use the restroom, Mom. - Okay.

2186
01:21:07,750 --> 01:21:09,060
It's quite filling, isn't it?

2187
01:21:09,760 --> 01:21:11,060
- Right. - I'm feeling full.

2188
01:21:14,230 --> 01:21:17,630
(He heads to the parking lot outside the restaurant.)

2189
01:21:20,300 --> 01:21:21,470
Finally!

2190
01:21:21,630 --> 01:21:22,640
(Bumping)

2191
01:21:23,000 --> 01:21:24,069
It must be a gift.

2192
01:21:24,070 --> 01:21:25,170
Gosh!

2193
01:21:25,310 --> 01:21:27,240
- He was in a hurry. - It's a gift for her?

2194
01:21:28,110 --> 01:21:29,440
My head is too big.

2195
01:21:32,410 --> 01:21:33,480
Gosh, it's cold.

2196
01:21:33,850 --> 01:21:35,450
I need some background music.

2197
01:21:36,120 --> 01:21:38,890
(He carefully returns after getting the things.)

2198
01:21:42,290 --> 01:21:44,090
(Peeking)

2199
01:21:45,960 --> 01:21:48,389
(Happy birthday to you)

2200
01:21:48,390 --> 01:21:49,960
(Confused)

2201
01:21:51,130 --> 01:21:52,629
- It's her birthday? - It's her birthday.

2202
01:21:52,630 --> 01:21:55,400
- I see. - Her birthday is on December 21.

2203
01:21:55,800 --> 01:21:57,669
I knew I wouldn't be able to see her that day,

2204
01:21:57,670 --> 01:21:59,109
so I wanted to throw her a surprise in advance...

2205
01:21:59,110 --> 01:22:01,039
while she came to visit.

2206
01:22:01,040 --> 01:22:03,540
Happy birthday to you

2207
01:22:04,210 --> 01:22:05,280
Gosh!

2208
01:22:05,810 --> 01:22:08,050
- What a lovely sight. - You should check what's inside.

2209
01:22:08,620 --> 01:22:09,719
Open it up.

2210
01:22:09,720 --> 01:22:11,020
(Curious)

2211
01:22:11,250 --> 01:22:13,650
"Happy birthday."

2212
01:22:13,950 --> 01:22:16,919
"Don't hide your joy after receiving the gift..."

2213
01:22:16,920 --> 01:22:18,159
"and make sure to show it."

2214
01:22:18,160 --> 01:22:19,660
It's my mom's birthday soon.

2215
01:22:20,160 --> 01:22:22,160
My small treasure.

2216
01:22:22,560 --> 01:22:23,829
Why are you her small treasure?

2217
01:22:23,830 --> 01:22:25,700
- Big treasure? - That's my older sister.

2218
01:22:26,500 --> 01:22:27,700
- Happy birthday! - Gosh.

2219
01:22:29,300 --> 01:22:31,340
- Thank you, my son. - It's for you.

2220
01:22:31,840 --> 01:22:33,910
- Gosh, thank you. - Open it up.

2221
01:22:34,270 --> 01:22:35,540
What do you think it is?

2222
01:22:35,740 --> 01:22:36,810
I wonder.

2223
01:22:36,980 --> 01:22:38,910
- What could it be? - What is it?

2224
01:22:40,550 --> 01:22:41,749
(Smiling brightly)

2225
01:22:41,750 --> 01:22:42,850
What is it?

2226
01:22:43,820 --> 01:22:44,879
What is that?

2227
01:22:44,880 --> 01:22:46,589
- My goodness! - It's money!

2228
01:22:46,590 --> 01:22:48,350
(A cake full of bills)

2229
01:22:50,160 --> 01:22:52,490
Did you prepare that in the morning?

2230
01:22:52,630 --> 01:22:54,390
I worked on it a bit the night before.

2231
01:22:54,660 --> 01:22:56,776
- You just finished it? - I just finished it in the morning.

2232
01:22:56,800 --> 01:22:59,300
My goodness!

2233
01:22:59,800 --> 01:23:01,700
- How much does this look like? - That's great.

2234
01:23:01,830 --> 01:23:03,939
I don't know. Does that really matter right now?

2235
01:23:03,940 --> 01:23:05,246
- Look here. - Of course, it matters.

2236
01:23:05,270 --> 01:23:07,670
- Right. - It has a golden bill as well.

2237
01:23:08,610 --> 01:23:09,839
- Is it 300 dollars? - You think it's 300 dollars?

2238
01:23:09,840 --> 01:23:10,840
Right.

2239
01:23:12,210 --> 01:23:13,249
It's less than that.

2240
01:23:13,250 --> 01:23:15,419
- No? Then it should be 250 dollars. - It's 270 dollars.

2241
01:23:15,420 --> 01:23:16,479
Gosh.

2242
01:23:16,480 --> 01:23:18,349
You should've filled it to be 300 dollars.

2243
01:23:18,350 --> 01:23:20,110
- Why 270 dollars? - I put in a golden bill.

2244
01:23:21,150 --> 01:23:22,759
- You should've gone up to 300. - Well,

2245
01:23:22,760 --> 01:23:25,529
there were only 23 pockets.

2246
01:23:25,530 --> 01:23:27,589
You could've forced in the bills to reach 300 dollars.

2247
01:23:27,590 --> 01:23:29,376
Or you should've put in 270 dollars in the cake...

2248
01:23:29,400 --> 01:23:31,059
and brought out the 30 dollars as a surprise.

2249
01:23:31,060 --> 01:23:32,900
- "Here they are!" - That would've been nice.

2250
01:23:33,670 --> 01:23:34,829
That makes it go up to 300.

2251
01:23:34,830 --> 01:23:36,739
Why won't you do that yourself with all of those ideas?

2252
01:23:36,740 --> 01:23:38,470
- Why? - I'll probably do that someday.

2253
01:23:39,510 --> 01:23:41,790
- I should try that. - Bring out the bills as a surprise.

2254
01:23:43,010 --> 01:23:44,140
But...

2255
01:23:44,340 --> 01:23:45,779
- there's another one. - There's another one.

2256
01:23:45,780 --> 01:23:48,479
- I divided it up. - You really wanted these.

2257
01:23:48,480 --> 01:23:49,480
I did?

2258
01:23:49,481 --> 01:23:50,579
The sneakers?

2259
01:23:50,580 --> 01:23:51,949
Shoes? Oh, they're sneakers.

2260
01:23:51,950 --> 01:23:53,350
- She likes sneakers? - Really?

2261
01:23:53,650 --> 01:23:54,749
- Gosh, they look lovely. - Really?

2262
01:23:54,750 --> 01:23:56,190
Check the grip as well.

2263
01:23:57,220 --> 01:23:59,289
She always mentioned them when we talked on the phone.

2264
01:23:59,290 --> 01:24:01,489
- "Your aunt said they were great." - She wanted them as well.

2265
01:24:01,490 --> 01:24:02,599
- She made it obvious. - She made it obvious.

2266
01:24:02,600 --> 01:24:04,959
Right. I kept thinking about them.

2267
01:24:04,960 --> 01:24:06,129
That was why.

2268
01:24:06,130 --> 01:24:08,800
(Laughing)

2269
01:24:09,300 --> 01:24:10,399
Slowly.

2270
01:24:10,400 --> 01:24:12,739
- The laces should be loosened. - Hold on.

2271
01:24:12,740 --> 01:24:13,840
But...

2272
01:24:14,810 --> 01:24:15,880
Try jumping.

2273
01:24:16,110 --> 01:24:17,639
Gosh, it feels great.

2274
01:24:17,640 --> 01:24:18,879
- She looks excited. - Try moving around.

2275
01:24:18,880 --> 01:24:20,479
- This brand... - The tone of her voice...

2276
01:24:20,480 --> 01:24:21,909
- definitely went up. - Right.

2277
01:24:21,910 --> 01:24:23,820
- It went right up. - There's a difference.

2278
01:24:23,950 --> 01:24:26,196
- There's certainly a difference. - I think you might not wear them.

2279
01:24:26,220 --> 01:24:27,489
It looks nice. Great.

2280
01:24:27,490 --> 01:24:28,760
Put on the left one as well.

2281
01:24:30,120 --> 01:24:31,789
(Smiling)

2282
01:24:31,790 --> 01:24:33,390
Come here, my son.

2283
01:24:35,230 --> 01:24:37,060
Thank you. I'll use them well.

2284
01:24:37,360 --> 01:24:38,999
I should stay healthy for a long time...

2285
01:24:39,000 --> 01:24:40,430
- to make you good food. - Right.

2286
01:24:41,430 --> 01:24:45,240
Let's go to Jeju Island at the start of next year.

2287
01:24:45,540 --> 01:24:46,640
Sure.

2288
01:24:46,910 --> 01:24:48,740
We'll go to Japan at the end of next year.

2289
01:24:49,380 --> 01:24:51,910
When was the last time you went to Jeju Island?

2290
01:24:52,180 --> 01:24:54,009
Has it been 50 years?

2291
01:24:54,010 --> 01:24:55,719
I went on a retreat when I was a junior in high school.

2292
01:24:55,720 --> 01:24:57,119
Right. You didn't go ever since that, right?

2293
01:24:57,120 --> 01:24:58,800
I've never been to Jeju Island after that.

2294
01:24:59,520 --> 01:25:01,720
We should travel together for a long time.

2295
01:25:02,690 --> 01:25:03,860
Let's travel together.

2296
01:25:04,460 --> 01:25:06,190
I'll be healthy for a long time.

2297
01:25:07,830 --> 01:25:08,900
Thank you.

2298
01:25:12,430 --> 01:25:13,600
Gosh.

2299
01:25:16,540 --> 01:25:18,810
Why cry? Have some water.

2300
01:25:20,110 --> 01:25:21,439
I thought I would cry if my mom cried.

2301
01:25:21,440 --> 01:25:23,640
I kept trying to distract her.

2302
01:25:23,840 --> 01:25:25,110
Great job.

2303
01:25:26,910 --> 01:25:30,080
I always think that...

2304
01:25:31,920 --> 01:25:33,550
I have to stay healthy.

2305
01:25:37,220 --> 01:25:38,489
Healthy people wouldn't do this,

2306
01:25:38,490 --> 01:25:40,930
but this is my prayer I give every morning I wake up.

2307
01:25:41,430 --> 01:25:43,030
"Thank you once again today."

2308
01:25:43,360 --> 01:25:46,170
"Thank you for allowing me to wake up in good health."

2309
01:25:52,440 --> 01:25:55,640
I always need to hear my mom's voice.

2310
01:25:56,180 --> 01:25:59,480
I want to treat my mom to the best food.

2311
01:26:00,050 --> 01:26:01,549
I want to give her the best clothes.

2312
01:26:01,550 --> 01:26:03,080
I want to take her to the best places.

2313
01:26:03,720 --> 01:26:06,150
I want to get her the best things in this world.

2314
01:26:07,250 --> 01:26:09,090
That's who she is to me.

2315
01:26:10,420 --> 01:26:12,830
Let's go to Jeju Island and Japan next year.

2316
01:26:13,030 --> 01:26:14,550
Let's travel together for a long time.

2317
01:26:14,730 --> 01:26:17,500
- Right. I have to stay healthy. - Happy birthday.

2318
01:26:18,030 --> 01:26:19,629
- Thank you, my son. - Happy birthday.

2319
01:26:19,630 --> 01:26:21,099
I'll stay healthy for a long time...

2320
01:26:21,100 --> 01:26:23,939
and not be a burden to you. Okay?

2321
01:26:23,940 --> 01:26:25,299
(The Mother and Son's Warm Winter Night)

2322
01:26:25,300 --> 01:26:26,840
(Next episode)

2323
01:26:27,670 --> 01:26:29,439
(Here's another great son.)

2324
01:26:29,440 --> 01:26:30,840
(Mom!)

2325
01:26:31,280 --> 01:26:32,810
